1
00:01:16,699 --> 00:01:18,865
<i>Dear Author,</i>

2
00:01:18,907 --> 00:01:21,032
<i>my name is Kim Dokja.</i>

3
00:01:22,449 --> 00:01:25,282
<i>I just read the last episode
that you uploaded today.</i>

4
00:01:28,032 --> 00:01:30,115
<i>Your web novel, TWSA,</i>

5
00:01:30,157 --> 00:01:32,282
<i>Three Ways to Survive
the Apocalypse,</i>

6
00:01:32,324 --> 00:01:34,115
<i>began its publication
when I was</i>

7
00:01:34,157 --> 00:01:35,865
<i>in my third year
of middle school.</i>

8
00:01:35,907 --> 00:01:40,615
Mammals include
humans, bears...

9
00:01:40,657 --> 00:01:43,449
<i>I still remember
that first sentence.</i>

10
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:46,407
<i>The subway car stopped
in the middle of Dongho Bridge.</i>

11
00:01:48,990 --> 00:01:51,490
<i>:
Planetary system 8612's</i>

12
00:01:51,532 --> 00:01:53,615
<i>free service has now ended.</i>

13
00:01:53,657 --> 00:01:55,782
<i>: To punish
fallen humanity,</i>

14
00:01:55,824 --> 00:01:58,157
<i>the gods sent down
terrible hardships.</i>

15
00:01:58,199 --> 00:02:00,324
<i>And as the world
neared complete collapse,</i>

16
00:02:00,365 --> 00:02:02,490
<i>the hero Yoo Junghyuk
and his companions</i>

17
00:02:02,532 --> 00:02:04,949
<i>overcame these deadly trials.</i>

18
00:02:07,199 --> 00:02:09,282
<i>At first,
TWSA was quite popular.</i>

19
00:02:09,324 --> 00:02:12,032
<i>But as the story went on,
people called it too extreme</i>

20
00:02:12,074 --> 00:02:13,532
<i>or unrealistic.</i>

21
00:02:13,574 --> 00:02:15,365
<i>Many stopped following
the story.</i>

22
00:02:23,115 --> 00:02:24,865
Hey! What's that?

23
00:02:24,907 --> 00:02:26,115
Let me see it!

24
00:02:26,157 --> 00:02:27,865
- Just let me see it!
- Give me my phone!

25
00:02:27,907 --> 00:02:29,240
Do you wanna die?

26
00:02:29,282 --> 00:02:30,865
<i>Still, during my school years,</i>

27
00:02:30,907 --> 00:02:32,365
<i>your story was everything to me.</i>

28
00:02:33,865 --> 00:02:35,074
<i>With every update,</i>

29
00:02:35,115 --> 00:02:36,782
<i>I'd reread the last two episodes</i>

30
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:37,990
<i>to keep the flow.</i>

31
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:39,115
<i>And on weekends,</i>

32
00:02:39,157 --> 00:02:41,282
<i>I reread the entire
week's episodes.</i>

33
00:02:41,324 --> 00:02:44,824
<i>And yes, when the views
fell to just one reader,</i>

34
00:02:44,865 --> 00:02:46,740
<i>that was me.</i>

35
00:02:47,990 --> 00:02:50,990
<i>Why read a novel for 10 years
when no one else was reading it?</i>

36
00:02:52,532 --> 00:02:53,949
<i>Yoo Junghyuk.</i>

37
00:02:54,407 --> 00:02:56,032
<i>I wanted to be him.</i>

38
00:03:01,615 --> 00:03:04,865
<i>Yoo and his companions brought
vicious enemies to their knees.</i>

39
00:03:05,657 --> 00:03:07,574
<i>And they never backed down,</i>

40
00:03:07,615 --> 00:03:10,032
<i>whether it be monsters
or humans alike.</i>

41
00:03:13,199 --> 00:03:14,740
Lee Hyeonseong!

42
00:03:14,782 --> 00:03:17,240
<i>But as his companions
fell one by one,</i>

43
00:03:17,865 --> 00:03:21,740
<i>to survive, Yoo Junghyuk
resolved to be stronger.</i>

44
00:03:25,865 --> 00:03:27,324
<i>And so he did.</i>

45
00:03:27,365 --> 00:03:29,657
<i>He got stronger and stronger,</i>

46
00:03:29,699 --> 00:03:31,282
<i>but as I entered high school,</i>

47
00:03:31,324 --> 00:03:32,615
<i>I stayed the same.</i>

48
00:03:32,657 --> 00:03:34,449
Now, you two are going
to fight each other.

49
00:03:34,490 --> 00:03:36,824
The loser will become
our doormat.

50
00:03:36,865 --> 00:03:38,824
But the winner gets his freedom.

51
00:03:39,615 --> 00:03:42,365
What? You can't even
fight to save yourself?

52
00:03:43,407 --> 00:03:45,907
Alright, fine.
Don't do it, then.

53
00:03:45,949 --> 00:03:47,990
But then,

54
00:03:48,032 --> 00:03:50,824
that just means both
of you losers are doormats.

55
00:03:50,865 --> 00:03:52,574
<i>If only...</i>

56
00:03:52,615 --> 00:03:55,115
<i>I could also get stronger.</i>

57
00:03:55,157 --> 00:03:56,490
<i>Like Yoo Junghyuk.</i>

58
00:03:57,949 --> 00:04:00,157
<i>That was always my wish.</i>

59
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:06,574
<i>I went to a mediocre college,</i>

60
00:04:06,615 --> 00:04:08,574
<i>worked a bunch of mediocre jobs,</i>

61
00:04:08,615 --> 00:04:10,282
<i>then I joined this company.</i>

62
00:04:10,324 --> 00:04:11,532
<i>On a temp contract.</i>

63
00:04:14,532 --> 00:04:16,490
<i>Today, the novel ended.</i>

64
00:04:17,073 --> 00:04:18,615
<i>And so did my contract.</i>

65
00:04:19,573 --> 00:04:21,115
Good work. Thanks, Dokja.

66
00:04:21,157 --> 00:04:23,449
Huh. Hey.
Call if you're in the area.

67
00:04:23,490 --> 00:04:24,615
I'll treat you.

68
00:04:24,657 --> 00:04:25,907
Thanks.

69
00:04:27,074 --> 00:04:29,199
This is why we shouldn't hire
these regional college grads.

70
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:31,324
Yeah.
They're not on our level.

71
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:35,865
<i>: I really appreciate
all your hard work</i>

72
00:04:35,907 --> 00:04:37,865
<i>writing this story
for so long.</i>

73
00:04:39,365 --> 00:04:40,740
<i>But I have to ask:</i>

74
00:04:42,032 --> 00:04:45,199
<i>Why'd you make Yoo Junghyuk
the only survivor at the end?</i>

75
00:04:48,365 --> 00:04:50,199
<i>What's the point of an ending</i>

76
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:52,365
<i>with only one survivor?</i>

77
00:04:54,865 --> 00:04:56,824
<i>Yoo Junghyuk once said,</i>

78
00:04:58,032 --> 00:05:00,990
<i>"I can't help it if others
are sacrificed so I can live."</i>

79
00:05:02,532 --> 00:05:04,407
<i>Is that the theme of the novel?</i>

80
00:05:05,949 --> 00:05:08,157
<i>If it is, I can't accept that.</i>

81
00:05:09,865 --> 00:05:12,699
<i>Sir, your novel...</i>

82
00:05:13,699 --> 00:05:15,324
<i>is the worst.</i>

83
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:20,157
<i>:
The train for Daehwa</i>

84
00:05:20,199 --> 00:05:21,574
<i>is approaching.</i>

85
00:05:21,615 --> 00:05:25,365
<i>Repeat. The train for Daehwa
is approaching.</i>

86
00:05:36,782 --> 00:05:38,782
Jeez, that was quite the sigh.

87
00:05:39,490 --> 00:05:41,865
Uh, hi... Sangah.

88
00:05:41,907 --> 00:05:44,949
Was it your last day, too?

89
00:05:44,990 --> 00:05:47,490
I knew they'd never
hire me full-time.

90
00:05:47,532 --> 00:05:51,115
No use fighting for something
that was never gonna be yours.

91
00:05:51,157 --> 00:05:53,657
Just need to move on
and find a job that suits me.

92
00:05:54,990 --> 00:05:57,490
Oh... thank you so much.

93
00:05:58,532 --> 00:06:01,615
Have you, uh,
already found a new job?

94
00:06:01,657 --> 00:06:03,449
Just a part-time one.

95
00:06:03,490 --> 00:06:04,907
Need to survive
the month somehow.

96
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:08,657
Hey, you know how I designed
all those character costumes?

97
00:06:08,699 --> 00:06:10,907
I felt that was something
I was really good at,

98
00:06:10,949 --> 00:06:13,324
so I think I wanna pursue
designing real clothes.

99
00:06:13,365 --> 00:06:15,865
Eventually launch my own brand
and open a shop.

100
00:06:15,907 --> 00:06:17,365
Cool, huh?

101
00:06:18,115 --> 00:06:19,657
That sounds really great,
Sangha.

102
00:06:19,699 --> 00:06:21,990
Oh, Sangha!

103
00:06:22,032 --> 00:06:24,907
- Fancy meeting you here.
- Uh, hey Mr. Han.

104
00:06:24,949 --> 00:06:26,615
Didn't I say I'd buy you
dinner tonight?

105
00:06:26,657 --> 00:06:28,282
Uh... thank you,
but I have plans.

106
00:06:28,324 --> 00:06:30,240
I gotta say, I'm disappointed

107
00:06:30,282 --> 00:06:32,157
our little Sangha
is leaving us.

108
00:06:32,199 --> 00:06:33,365
You know,

109
00:06:33,407 --> 00:06:34,949
if you'd given me a chance,

110
00:06:34,990 --> 00:06:37,157
I'd have fought harder
to get you hired.

111
00:06:37,199 --> 00:06:38,490
Oh, don't worry about it.

112
00:06:38,532 --> 00:06:39,949
I don't think my skills
were there yet.

113
00:06:39,990 --> 00:06:41,824
What do you say we
get off this train

114
00:06:41,865 --> 00:06:43,240
and maybe grab that dinner?

115
00:06:43,282 --> 00:06:44,907
I know a nice place
in Apgujeong.

116
00:06:44,949 --> 00:06:46,990
Oh. Uh, I'm heading
to my part-time job.

117
00:06:47,032 --> 00:06:49,907
Hey, no excuses.
I'll pay for the hours you miss.

118
00:06:49,949 --> 00:06:53,074
Uh... that's really okay, sir.

119
00:06:53,115 --> 00:06:55,615
I'm actually seeing someone.

120
00:06:56,199 --> 00:06:58,282
Ah. Is this him?

121
00:06:58,782 --> 00:07:00,615
Uh, hello, Mr. Han.

122
00:07:00,657 --> 00:07:03,157
Uh, we've met. I'm Kim Dokja
from map development.

123
00:07:03,824 --> 00:07:05,074
Huh.

124
00:07:06,574 --> 00:07:09,407
So, you two have had something
going on all this time?

125
00:07:09,449 --> 00:07:11,240
Well. That's disappointing.

126
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:14,782
<i>:
Our next stop is Apgujeong.</i>

127
00:07:14,824 --> 00:07:16,449
<i>Apgujeong.</i>

128
00:07:16,490 --> 00:07:18,324
<i>The doors are on your right.</i>

129
00:07:18,365 --> 00:07:19,949
Enjoy your dinner, sir.

130
00:07:19,990 --> 00:07:21,657
<i>- Please stand clear.</i>
- Thanks, Sangha.

131
00:07:21,699 --> 00:07:23,532
I'll see you around, I guess.

132
00:07:23,574 --> 00:07:25,657
<i>We are not
responsible for any...</i>

133
00:07:27,157 --> 00:07:29,282
God.
That guy is such a creep.

134
00:07:29,324 --> 00:07:31,157
I couldn't even report him
'cause I was worried about...

135
00:07:31,199 --> 00:07:33,365
...getting fired.

136
00:07:33,407 --> 00:07:34,990
That was smart.

137
00:07:35,032 --> 00:07:36,740
Silence is golden.

138
00:07:36,782 --> 00:07:38,449
Oh, please.
I wasn't being smart.

139
00:07:38,490 --> 00:07:39,949
I was being an idiot.

140
00:07:39,990 --> 00:07:41,782
And that's what's so
frustrating about it.

141
00:07:41,824 --> 00:07:43,240
I knew I should've
said something,

142
00:07:43,282 --> 00:07:45,115
but I didn't
because I'm a coward.

143
00:07:45,157 --> 00:07:46,699
Huh? You see how
frustrating that is?

144
00:08:00,157 --> 00:08:01,949
Sorry. Just give me a minute.

145
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,074
<i>:
The doors are now closing.</i>

146
00:08:15,032 --> 00:08:16,449
{\an8}

147
00:08:18,865 --> 00:08:21,407
- Your girlfriend?
- Oh. No.

148
00:08:42,032 --> 00:08:43,782
<i>: The ending I want?</i>

149
00:08:44,574 --> 00:08:45,615
<i>What does that even mean?</i>

150
00:08:45,657 --> 00:08:47,157
<i>Next stop, Oksu.</i>

151
00:08:47,199 --> 00:08:49,657
Oh. Thank you, miss.

152
00:08:51,574 --> 00:08:54,407
<i>: Readers' submissions
at seven PM.</i>

153
00:08:54,449 --> 00:08:56,240
<i>But I was the only reader.</i>

154
00:08:57,657 --> 00:08:59,907
<i>Does that mean
I can change the ending?</i>

155
00:09:12,532 --> 00:09:13,824
Are you okay?

156
00:09:13,865 --> 00:09:16,074
<i>:
Planetary system 8612's</i>

157
00:09:16,115 --> 00:09:18,282
<i>free service has now ended.</i>

158
00:09:18,324 --> 00:09:21,282
<i>This is the beginning
of paid content.</i>

159
00:09:22,532 --> 00:09:24,365
<i>I repeat.</i>

160
00:09:24,407 --> 00:09:27,074
<i>Planetary system 8612's</i>

161
00:09:27,115 --> 00:09:29,449
<i>free service has now ended.</i>

162
00:09:29,490 --> 00:09:32,865
<i>This is the beginning
of paid content.</i>

163
00:09:32,907 --> 00:09:34,907
<i>: Is this actually...</i>

164
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,865
<i>"An announcement echoes
through the air,</i>

165
00:09:36,907 --> 00:09:38,699
<i>planetary system 8612's</i>

166
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:40,449
<i>free service has now ended.</i>

167
00:09:40,490 --> 00:09:43,032
<i>This is the beginning
of paid content.</i>

168
00:09:43,074 --> 00:09:45,449
<i>This one fellow who
I'll call a Dokkaebi..."</i>

169
00:09:45,490 --> 00:09:47,907
<i>What? A Dokkaebi?</i>

170
00:09:50,782 --> 00:09:52,365
What the hell
is going on?

171
00:09:53,782 --> 00:09:55,324
<i>- Oh, my God...</i>

172
00:09:55,365 --> 00:09:57,490
<i>This is just like
the start of the novel.</i>

173
00:09:57,532 --> 00:10:01,157
Hello! The language patch
is now working. Ha!

174
00:10:01,199 --> 00:10:03,615
People. Can you hear me?

175
00:10:03,657 --> 00:10:05,740
Oh, Jesus Christ, man.
What is this?

176
00:10:05,782 --> 00:10:08,240
Yes. I understand
your frustration.

177
00:10:08,282 --> 00:10:09,782
I know you're all busy,

178
00:10:09,824 --> 00:10:12,032
but I still require
your attention

179
00:10:12,074 --> 00:10:13,324
for a moment--

180
00:10:13,365 --> 00:10:14,615
Enough of this
crap already!

181
00:10:14,657 --> 00:10:16,949
Get this train moving!
This is unacceptable!

182
00:10:16,990 --> 00:10:18,324
I'll have to ask you
to quiet down.

183
00:10:18,365 --> 00:10:22,032
You need to listen to what
I'm about to tell you all.

184
00:10:22,074 --> 00:10:24,699
'Cause I assure you all,
it's of the utmost importance!

185
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:26,990
Why don't you shut the hell up
and get us out of here

186
00:10:27,032 --> 00:10:28,782
before I lose my shit on you?

187
00:10:28,824 --> 00:10:30,574
I got a bunch of shit
to get done

188
00:10:30,615 --> 00:10:31,990
and you guys stop
the train for this?

189
00:10:32,032 --> 00:10:33,949
You're nothing but a bunch
of stupid ass--

190
00:10:41,365 --> 00:10:44,490
I said quiet!

191
00:10:47,657 --> 00:10:49,032
Now, humans,

192
00:10:49,074 --> 00:10:51,240
I want you to listen closely

193
00:10:51,282 --> 00:10:53,782
to every word I say to you.

194
00:10:53,824 --> 00:10:56,657
High up in space,
watching with cruel amusement

195
00:10:56,699 --> 00:10:59,574
are celestial beings
far greater than any human.

196
00:10:59,615 --> 00:11:02,407
And they have, at last,
come to a decision.

197
00:11:02,449 --> 00:11:05,615
That humans, the most
vulgar, greedy, pathetic,

198
00:11:05,657 --> 00:11:08,949
self-centred race
in the whole universe

199
00:11:08,990 --> 00:11:10,532
must all be punished!

200
00:11:10,574 --> 00:11:13,282
<i>:
Channel BI-7623 has opened.</i>

201
00:11:13,324 --> 00:11:14,782
<i>Constellations are entering.</i>

202
00:11:14,824 --> 00:11:16,490
Welcome, dear Constellations!

203
00:11:16,532 --> 00:11:19,324
Some very interesting things
are about to happen.

204
00:11:19,365 --> 00:11:21,074
So, please enjoy!

205
00:11:21,115 --> 00:11:23,032
From this moment on,

206
00:11:23,074 --> 00:11:25,990
all you humans will be
given a scenario.

207
00:11:27,699 --> 00:11:32,115
And how you solve that scenario
will help determine your fate.

208
00:11:32,157 --> 00:11:34,324
<i>The first main scenario</i>

209
00:11:34,365 --> 00:11:35,740
<i>is starting.</i>

210
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:42,074
Since this is your first time,
I'll explain it to you.

211
00:11:42,115 --> 00:11:44,282
Kill one or more
living organisms

212
00:11:44,324 --> 00:11:47,574
in this subway car
within 10 minutes.

213
00:11:47,615 --> 00:11:50,449
Succeed and you each
get 300 coins.

214
00:11:50,490 --> 00:11:52,907
Fail and you'll end up
like that poor soul.

215
00:11:52,949 --> 00:11:54,657
Simple. Huh?

216
00:11:54,699 --> 00:11:58,407
Our dear Constellations will be
watching it all unfold closely,

217
00:11:58,449 --> 00:12:01,157
so pay no heed
to laws or ethics.

218
00:12:01,199 --> 00:12:04,365
Just show us without reservation

219
00:12:04,407 --> 00:12:07,532
the true nature of you humans.

220
00:12:30,282 --> 00:12:31,824
Our phones aren't working,
right?

221
00:12:31,865 --> 00:12:33,032
No. They're not gonna work.

222
00:12:39,782 --> 00:12:41,990
Are you alone?
Are your parents here?

223
00:12:43,199 --> 00:12:44,782
Are you gonna kill me?

224
00:12:47,115 --> 00:12:48,324
Oh, my God!

225
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,782
<i>: Yoo Junghyuk?</i>

226
00:13:26,865 --> 00:13:28,157
<i>This is crazy.</i>

227
00:13:28,199 --> 00:13:29,532
<i>A novel that only I've read</i>

228
00:13:29,574 --> 00:13:31,490
<i>has become a reality.</i>

229
00:13:31,532 --> 00:13:33,282
<i>That means I know the future.</i>

230
00:13:34,199 --> 00:13:36,574
<i>Wait... then next is...</i>

231
00:13:58,532 --> 00:14:00,824
<i>First, I have to beat
this scenario.</i>

232
00:14:00,865 --> 00:14:03,615
<i>Let me think.
One or more living organisms.</i>

233
00:14:03,657 --> 00:14:05,907
<i>One or more living organisms...</i>

234
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:24,657
Sangha.

235
00:14:25,824 --> 00:14:28,407
Hang onto this.
I'm gonna go save the others.

236
00:14:28,449 --> 00:14:31,240
Where are you going?
Are you crazy?

237
00:14:31,282 --> 00:14:33,074
You'll die if you go there!

238
00:14:33,115 --> 00:14:35,865
I know this.

239
00:14:35,907 --> 00:14:37,865
- Huh?
- I think I know

240
00:14:37,907 --> 00:14:39,449
how to solve this.

241
00:14:46,865 --> 00:14:48,824
Hey! Everyone! Listen up!

242
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:53,740
People! Listen to me
for a minute!

243
00:14:55,324 --> 00:14:56,865
I know what to do!

244
00:15:10,282 --> 00:15:13,782
<i>: The first kill
on this car has taken place.</i>

245
00:15:13,824 --> 00:15:16,574
<i>The killer will now
receive 300 coins.</i>

246
00:15:17,907 --> 00:15:21,282
What? Wait.
How did you do that, huh?

247
00:15:21,990 --> 00:15:23,990
It said we've all gotta kill

248
00:15:24,032 --> 00:15:27,574
one or more living organisms,
right?

249
00:15:27,615 --> 00:15:29,699
It said...

250
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:31,532
living organism.

251
00:15:31,574 --> 00:15:33,532
It didn't say humans.

252
00:15:33,574 --> 00:15:35,490
Wait, wait! Stop.

253
00:15:35,532 --> 00:15:36,865
Hold on. Don't come closer.

254
00:15:36,907 --> 00:15:38,532
Stop.
Stop or I'll kill them all!

255
00:15:38,574 --> 00:15:40,449
Wait, don't! Wait!

256
00:15:40,490 --> 00:15:42,615
How many ants are in that thing?
Tell us that.

257
00:15:45,657 --> 00:15:46,990
Let me see.

258
00:15:48,199 --> 00:15:49,532
Not enough for everyone.

259
00:15:50,365 --> 00:15:52,157
Hey, buddy!
If there's not enough,

260
00:15:52,199 --> 00:15:53,615
you should've said so.

261
00:15:53,657 --> 00:15:55,324
Why'd you kill one
before saying anything?

262
00:15:55,365 --> 00:15:56,949
How do we decide who gets one?

263
00:15:56,990 --> 00:15:58,574
We should give them
to the kids first.

264
00:15:58,615 --> 00:16:00,074
Hey, hey! Shut up, lady!

265
00:16:00,115 --> 00:16:01,865
Everyone's life is worth
the same thing here, okay?

266
00:16:01,907 --> 00:16:03,740
Your kid's life
is not more important!

267
00:16:03,782 --> 00:16:05,907
Everyone, calm down.
Look, I wish I had enough

268
00:16:05,949 --> 00:16:08,407
- for everyone, but I...
- So? What do we do?

269
00:16:08,449 --> 00:16:10,240
There's no time.
We need to hurry!

270
00:16:10,282 --> 00:16:12,282
Hold on. Hold on!

271
00:16:12,324 --> 00:16:14,199
This guy works for me.
I'm his boss.

272
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,657
Let me through. Just a minute.

273
00:16:18,907 --> 00:16:21,740
Okay, look. Why are you making
the call on this?

274
00:16:21,782 --> 00:16:24,949
There are people here with way
more life experience than you.

275
00:16:24,990 --> 00:16:26,615
So give it.

276
00:16:26,657 --> 00:16:29,240
Yeah, that might be true,
but people here--

277
00:16:29,282 --> 00:16:31,157
Trust me. I know
how to do this properly.

278
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:33,074
Just give it to me!

279
00:16:33,115 --> 00:16:34,907
Hey, back off!

280
00:16:45,782 --> 00:16:47,240
Come on! Why won't you die?

281
00:16:49,032 --> 00:16:50,657
Sheesh! Just die already!

282
00:16:56,282 --> 00:16:58,074
The hell's wrong with you?

283
00:16:58,115 --> 00:16:59,574
You wanna get yourself killed?

284
00:16:59,615 --> 00:17:02,990
Here. Both you and her
can live, okay?

285
00:17:04,615 --> 00:17:07,073
I've got my own ant.
Right here.

286
00:17:07,115 --> 00:17:09,990
A pathetic, useless insect.

287
00:17:10,032 --> 00:17:13,698
<i>In the novel, Kim Namwoon
is part of Yoo Junghyuk's team.</i>

288
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:15,073
<i>Was he always like this?</i>

289
00:17:15,115 --> 00:17:16,490
- Hey!
- Get off!

290
00:17:18,115 --> 00:17:20,948
Alright then. Maybe I'll
just kill you instead.

291
00:17:29,740 --> 00:17:32,574
<i>Wait. If this is really
just like the novel...</i>

292
00:17:34,449 --> 00:17:36,365
<i>Spend 300 coins on strength.</i>

293
00:17:36,407 --> 00:17:39,074
<i>: 300 coins
have been spent on strength.</i>

294
00:17:39,115 --> 00:17:40,949
<i>Strength is now increased.</i>

295
00:17:49,324 --> 00:17:51,990
You son of a bitch...
Now you're a dead man.

296
00:17:52,032 --> 00:17:53,699
<i>: Kim Namwoon
has activated</i>

297
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,282
<i>the Grim Dark Awakening skill.</i>

298
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:57,157
<i>: In the novel,
Namwoon was first to receive</i>

299
00:17:57,199 --> 00:17:58,740
<i>the Constellation's support.</i>

300
00:17:58,782 --> 00:18:00,365
<i>But why a guy like him?</i>

301
00:18:14,365 --> 00:18:17,615
Ah... Got some skills.
This is cool as hell!

302
00:18:17,657 --> 00:18:20,532
If you wanna save the old lady,

303
00:18:20,574 --> 00:18:22,240
then you have to die.

304
00:18:30,990 --> 00:18:33,907
<i>Are the ant eggs
living organisms, too?</i>

305
00:18:35,824 --> 00:18:38,032
<i>: One organism
killed.</i>

306
00:18:38,074 --> 00:18:40,824
<i>300 coins paid as a reward.</i>

307
00:18:47,157 --> 00:18:49,324
<i>: Spend 3,000 coins
on stamina.</i>

308
00:18:52,949 --> 00:18:54,990
<i>Spend 3,000 coins on agility.</i>

309
00:19:07,574 --> 00:19:09,740
{\an8}

310
00:19:11,865 --> 00:19:13,324
Wait. Wait!

311
00:19:13,365 --> 00:19:14,657
Okay.

312
00:19:14,699 --> 00:19:16,407
I won't hurt the old lady.

313
00:19:16,449 --> 00:19:19,199
- Just give me an ant.
- I've changed my mind.

314
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,282
I don't want you
in this story anymore.

315
00:19:21,324 --> 00:19:23,115
What the hell
are you talking about?

316
00:19:25,699 --> 00:19:27,824
Get off! Move!

317
00:19:29,115 --> 00:19:31,240
Hey! Out of the way!

318
00:19:31,282 --> 00:19:33,324
Out of the way!
Come on, move!

319
00:19:33,365 --> 00:19:36,199
Move!

320
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,657
Get away from her!

321
00:19:37,699 --> 00:19:39,907
Argh! Come on!

322
00:19:42,449 --> 00:19:43,699
I'll keep going. I swear to God!

323
00:19:47,074 --> 00:19:48,532
<i>: Time has expired.</i>

324
00:19:48,574 --> 00:19:50,240
<i>The scenario has ended.</i>

325
00:20:04,824 --> 00:20:06,574
Ma'am. Ma'am!

326
00:20:06,615 --> 00:20:09,324
Excuse me, please wake up.
Ma'am?

327
00:20:18,699 --> 00:20:19,824
Dokja?

328
00:20:22,324 --> 00:20:24,240
Hey, are you okay?

329
00:20:38,490 --> 00:20:41,490
Ta-da! We wish
to give a heartfelt congrats

330
00:20:41,532 --> 00:20:45,574
to all of the 17 humans
who cleared the first scenario!

331
00:20:45,615 --> 00:20:48,115
You were supposed
to kill each other.

332
00:20:48,157 --> 00:20:51,949
But killing the ants wasn't
technically against the rules.

333
00:20:51,990 --> 00:20:54,657
The Constellations said that
this car was more fun to watch

334
00:20:54,699 --> 00:20:57,699
than the others.
So I guess we better move on.

335
00:20:57,740 --> 00:20:59,740
Now, for the Constellations

336
00:20:59,782 --> 00:21:01,657
to review and determine
amongst themselves

337
00:21:01,699 --> 00:21:04,324
which of you will receive
the Constellations' support.

338
00:21:04,365 --> 00:21:07,490
The Constellations' support
is a tremendous gift.

339
00:21:07,532 --> 00:21:09,699
If you choose well,
it'll be a big help

340
00:21:09,740 --> 00:21:11,699
in clearing future scenarios!

341
00:21:15,032 --> 00:21:16,407
<i>: "Thanks
to your actions,</i>

342
00:21:16,449 --> 00:21:17,615
<i>the following Constellations</i>

343
00:21:17,657 --> 00:21:19,282
<i>wish to give you their support."</i>

344
00:21:19,324 --> 00:21:22,490
Support? Constellations?
What does this mean?

345
00:21:22,532 --> 00:21:25,574
{\an8}<i>The Constellations watch over
all the scenarios</i>

346
00:21:25,615 --> 00:21:27,407
<i>from all the way
out in space.</i>

347
00:21:28,907 --> 00:21:31,365
<i>They enjoy laughing
at the struggles of humans</i>

348
00:21:31,407 --> 00:21:33,115
<i>who are trying to survive.</i>

349
00:21:33,157 --> 00:21:35,365
<i>If you're chosen to receive
their support,</i>

350
00:21:35,407 --> 00:21:37,449
<i>it can be very helpful.</i>

351
00:21:37,490 --> 00:21:39,074
<i>But eventually,</i>

352
00:21:39,115 --> 00:21:41,032
<i>that debt must be paid back.</i>

353
00:22:03,532 --> 00:22:05,949
Quick! Come to this side.

354
00:22:05,990 --> 00:22:07,199
Quick!

355
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:25,949
<i>Lee Hyeonseong.</i>

356
00:22:25,990 --> 00:22:28,574
<i>He's another character
who fought with Yoo Junghyuk.</i>

357
00:22:32,407 --> 00:22:34,199
Listen, don't waste
your strength.

358
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:36,532
- Use your skill.
- My skill?

359
00:22:36,574 --> 00:22:37,782
How the hell do I do that?

360
00:22:37,824 --> 00:22:39,240
At the bottom right
of your vision

361
00:22:39,282 --> 00:22:40,449
there's a skill window.

362
00:22:40,490 --> 00:22:41,990
If you just think hard about
your skill,

363
00:22:42,032 --> 00:22:43,365
it should work.

364
00:22:57,407 --> 00:22:59,407
<i>: Lee Hyeonseong
has activated</i>

365
00:22:59,449 --> 00:23:01,824
<i>Great Mountain Push level one.</i>

366
00:23:04,865 --> 00:23:06,324
Out of the way. Move.

367
00:23:18,699 --> 00:23:21,699
As soon as you're out,
get yourself across the bridge!

368
00:23:21,740 --> 00:23:22,907
Fast as you can!

369
00:23:22,949 --> 00:23:24,574
I'm Lee Hyeonseong.

370
00:23:24,615 --> 00:23:26,699
I'm Kim Dokja.
You better go.

371
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:34,865
Ahh!

372
00:23:45,490 --> 00:23:48,657
What are you doing?
Hey, hurry! We have to go.

373
00:23:53,949 --> 00:23:55,824
Ah! Ugh...

374
00:23:55,865 --> 00:23:57,699
Ugh, goddamnit.

375
00:24:00,074 --> 00:24:01,615
We need to go. Come on.

376
00:24:03,615 --> 00:24:05,824
Don't cry. It's okay.

377
00:24:05,865 --> 00:24:07,240
But we need to go right now.

378
00:24:07,282 --> 00:24:08,907
What's your name?

379
00:24:08,949 --> 00:24:11,574
- Lee Gilyeong.
- Hmm, Gilyeong.

380
00:24:11,615 --> 00:24:13,240
Can you run fast, Gilyeong?

381
00:24:13,282 --> 00:24:14,615
Wait...

382
00:24:14,657 --> 00:24:18,490
My ant farm got destroyed
because of you...

383
00:24:18,532 --> 00:24:20,324
I know.

384
00:24:20,365 --> 00:24:22,657
I'm really sorry about that,
but we really need to--

385
00:24:22,699 --> 00:24:26,490
No. My mom says apologizing
isn't always enough.

386
00:24:26,532 --> 00:24:29,282
You should take responsibility.

387
00:25:00,865 --> 00:25:03,157
<i>: A sub scenario
has arrived.</i>

388
00:25:03,199 --> 00:25:05,365
<i>Cross the severed bridge.</i>

389
00:25:05,407 --> 00:25:07,949
Why are they calling it
a severed bridge when it's not?

390
00:25:07,990 --> 00:25:09,657
'Cause it's about to be!

391
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:32,615
This is so exciting,

392
00:25:32,657 --> 00:25:34,990
but you can't just stand there,
you fools!

393
00:25:35,032 --> 00:25:37,282
I'll raise the difficulty level!

394
00:25:37,324 --> 00:25:38,699
Ahh!

395
00:25:48,032 --> 00:25:49,449
Argh!

396
00:25:54,282 --> 00:25:56,157
Argh!

397
00:26:02,824 --> 00:26:05,324
Dokja!
How is that even possible?

398
00:26:05,365 --> 00:26:07,490
I just thought of that
and it appeared out of nowhere,

399
00:26:07,532 --> 00:26:09,032
almost like I summoned it.

400
00:26:09,074 --> 00:26:10,990
Perfect! I'll go first!

401
00:26:11,657 --> 00:26:12,865
Lee Hyeonseong!

402
00:26:17,990 --> 00:26:19,740
Sangha!

403
00:26:20,865 --> 00:26:22,782
You chose a sponsor, right?

404
00:26:22,824 --> 00:26:25,865
Your sponsor is helping you.
Come on, let's move, Sangha.

405
00:26:27,782 --> 00:26:29,615
Soon, poisonous gas
will start to spread.

406
00:26:29,657 --> 00:26:31,615
We need to get underground
quickly.

407
00:26:32,365 --> 00:26:35,199
And make sure to collect coins!
That's really important!

408
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:37,115
How do you know all this?

409
00:26:37,157 --> 00:26:39,324
Let's just get
to the subway station.

410
00:26:39,365 --> 00:26:41,490
<i>Geumho station is the closest.</i>

411
00:26:41,532 --> 00:26:43,282
<i>If we take the same subway
station Yoo took,</i>

412
00:26:43,324 --> 00:26:44,490
<i>we should be safe.</i>

413
00:26:44,532 --> 00:26:46,115
<i>Wait.</i>

414
00:26:46,157 --> 00:26:47,990
<i>But at Chungmuro station...</i>

415
00:26:49,990 --> 00:26:51,407
<i>Early in the novel,</i>

416
00:26:51,449 --> 00:26:52,699
<i>Yoo died at Chungmuro station</i>

417
00:26:52,740 --> 00:26:53,949
<i>fighting the fire dragon.</i>

418
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:58,532
<i>Yoo used his Regression skill</i>

419
00:26:58,574 --> 00:27:00,699
<i>to go back to the beginning
of the story.</i>

420
00:27:01,407 --> 00:27:03,990
<i>But in a world without a hero</i>

421
00:27:04,032 --> 00:27:05,949
<i>everyone disappears.</i>

422
00:27:10,199 --> 00:27:13,282
<i>The hero must not die.</i>

423
00:27:14,615 --> 00:27:17,407
<i>But even with
the tactics I know</i>

424
00:27:17,449 --> 00:27:20,157
<i>one can't defeat
the fire dragon alone.</i>

425
00:27:32,699 --> 00:27:35,115
This is so tedious.

426
00:27:53,990 --> 00:27:55,282
<i>What if...</i>

427
00:27:55,324 --> 00:27:57,699
<i>I tell Yoo Junghyuk
those tactics?</i>

428
00:27:58,782 --> 00:28:00,574
<i>And we can fight together?</i>

429
00:28:01,574 --> 00:28:04,199
Dokja! Come on, hurry!

430
00:28:04,240 --> 00:28:06,282
Wait. I'll be there in a sec!

431
00:28:08,157 --> 00:28:09,657
Hey, Yoo Junghyuk!

432
00:28:27,865 --> 00:28:29,240
What are you?

433
00:28:31,324 --> 00:28:32,407
Uh, well...

434
00:28:32,449 --> 00:28:35,157
Kim Namwoon
shouldn't die this soon.

435
00:28:36,199 --> 00:28:38,699
- Did you kill him?
- No.

436
00:28:38,740 --> 00:28:40,407
No, I swear I didn't kill him.

437
00:28:40,449 --> 00:28:42,074
<i>: Yoo Junghyuk
has activated</i>

438
00:28:42,115 --> 00:28:43,740
<i>the Lie Detection skill.</i>

439
00:28:46,365 --> 00:28:47,740
Interesting.

440
00:28:47,782 --> 00:28:49,907
You already know
how to use coins.

441
00:28:49,949 --> 00:28:52,907
It's... not that, I just...

442
00:28:52,949 --> 00:28:54,490
Mr. Dokja!

443
00:28:54,532 --> 00:28:56,407
Are you okay?

444
00:28:56,449 --> 00:28:58,240
Yeah, I'm fine.
Just stay there.

445
00:28:58,282 --> 00:29:00,740
I'm really okay!
Please stay!

446
00:29:00,782 --> 00:29:03,282
And you know Lee Hyeonseong.

447
00:29:04,824 --> 00:29:07,657
Uh... I just met him
earlier today.

448
00:29:07,699 --> 00:29:09,199
I'll ask you again.

449
00:29:10,199 --> 00:29:11,490
What are you?

450
00:29:11,532 --> 00:29:15,115
If I tell him that I read
all this in a novel,

451
00:29:15,157 --> 00:29:17,365
he'll never believe me, right?

452
00:29:19,990 --> 00:29:21,740
My name is Kim Dokja.

453
00:29:21,782 --> 00:29:24,532
In a few days, you'll die
fighting the fire dragon.

454
00:29:24,574 --> 00:29:26,240
In Chungmuro station.

455
00:29:26,282 --> 00:29:27,990
Even if you regress,
it'll take a long time

456
00:29:28,032 --> 00:29:29,532
to clear the scenario.

457
00:29:29,574 --> 00:29:32,949
But if we go together,
you can defeat the fire dragon.

458
00:29:34,115 --> 00:29:35,657
I know the tactics you need.

459
00:29:35,699 --> 00:29:37,324
<i>: Yoo Junghyuk
has activated</i>

460
00:29:37,365 --> 00:29:39,407
<i>the Lie Detection skill.</i>

461
00:29:44,324 --> 00:29:46,282
How do you know
about those tactics?

462
00:29:48,740 --> 00:29:51,907
My personal skill is prophecy.

463
00:29:51,949 --> 00:29:56,324
So if you take me with you,
you can beat all the scenarios.

464
00:29:56,365 --> 00:29:57,699
Let's cross the bridge.

465
00:29:57,740 --> 00:29:59,740
You'll go via Geumho station,
right?

466
00:29:59,782 --> 00:30:01,407
- Hey, Kim Dokja.
- Yes?

467
00:30:04,324 --> 00:30:06,532
Wait! Please!
Why are you doing this?

468
00:30:06,574 --> 00:30:08,324
Tell me about the tactics.

469
00:30:08,365 --> 00:30:10,324
We can just go together
and beat the scenario!

470
00:30:11,824 --> 00:30:13,990
I can't stand dragging
people along.

471
00:30:14,032 --> 00:30:16,657
But if I tell you,
you're just gonna drop me.

472
00:30:16,699 --> 00:30:18,199
I'll drop you anyway.

473
00:30:18,240 --> 00:30:20,657
Wait! Please wait! Wait!

474
00:30:20,699 --> 00:30:23,824
Mr. Yoo, I have a terrible
fear of heights!

475
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:28,199
Ah! Please!
I'm just trying to help!

476
00:30:28,240 --> 00:30:30,532
First, let go!
Wait! No, no, no! Don't let go!

477
00:30:30,574 --> 00:30:33,074
Ah!

478
00:30:33,115 --> 00:30:35,032
Last chance.

479
00:30:35,074 --> 00:30:37,115
Why is all this happening?

480
00:30:38,699 --> 00:30:43,032
Why are humans
suddenly being punished?

481
00:30:44,740 --> 00:30:47,615
How... do you expect
me to know?

482
00:30:51,490 --> 00:30:54,490
Survive and come to Chungmuro.
Then you'll know.

483
00:30:54,532 --> 00:30:59,282
And then I'll decide
if I'm gonna fight with you.

484
00:31:04,365 --> 00:31:07,782
Yoo Junghyuk! You bastard!

485
00:31:09,074 --> 00:31:12,365
<i>In a few days, Yoo will die
fighting the fire dragon.</i>

486
00:31:13,365 --> 00:31:15,407
<i>But for me to live,</i>

487
00:31:15,449 --> 00:31:18,282
<i>the hero of the story
cannot die.</i>

488
00:31:20,615 --> 00:31:22,615
<i>But before any of that...</i>

489
00:31:24,199 --> 00:31:25,782
<i>I'm gonna die.</i>

490
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:53,282
<i>: A hidden scenario
has been unlocked.</i>

491
00:31:54,657 --> 00:31:58,324
<i>Kill the Ichthyosaur
and escape from its stomach.</i>

492
00:32:04,907 --> 00:32:06,657
I have to kill it to escape?

493
00:32:07,782 --> 00:32:09,240
Oh, shit!

494
00:32:09,282 --> 00:32:10,907
I don't have any items.

495
00:32:10,949 --> 00:32:14,949
Huh?
Huh? He's alive? He's alive!

496
00:32:14,990 --> 00:32:17,282
Constellations,
as you can no doubt see,

497
00:32:17,324 --> 00:32:20,199
a human has entered
the Ichthyosaur's belly.

498
00:32:20,240 --> 00:32:21,699
This is a truly...

499
00:32:21,740 --> 00:32:23,615
<i>: If I get on
the Dokkaebi's good side,</i>

500
00:32:23,657 --> 00:32:26,407
<i>he can help me get coins
or an item.</i>

501
00:32:26,449 --> 00:32:28,657
<i>And the thing a Dokkaebi
likes most of all...</i>

502
00:32:28,699 --> 00:32:31,615
...a human surprises us.
Am I right, Constellations?

503
00:32:31,657 --> 00:32:34,074
Hey! Get over here.

504
00:32:34,115 --> 00:32:36,199
Oh. The human's talking to me.

505
00:32:36,240 --> 00:32:39,324
I better get closer.
You lowly human.

506
00:32:39,365 --> 00:32:42,699
You are quite a sight
playing God with that ant farm.

507
00:32:42,740 --> 00:32:44,740
And you were
really terrifying, huh?

508
00:32:44,782 --> 00:32:46,907
Shooting people
with that little laser.

509
00:32:46,949 --> 00:32:48,532
You will speak to me

510
00:32:48,574 --> 00:32:49,782
with more respect.

511
00:32:49,824 --> 00:32:51,907
Yeah, well,
if you don't like it,

512
00:32:51,949 --> 00:32:53,949
why don't you just
shoot me then?

513
00:32:55,865 --> 00:32:59,990
How dare a foolish human
speak to a Dokkaebi this way?

514
00:33:00,032 --> 00:33:01,990
- Hey, Bihyung.
- Huh?

515
00:33:02,032 --> 00:33:03,865
You're doing
a star stream now, right?

516
00:33:03,907 --> 00:33:07,407
What the... You know my name?

517
00:33:07,449 --> 00:33:09,699
And how do you know
about star steams?

518
00:33:09,740 --> 00:33:11,782
Your channel
must be exploding now.

519
00:33:11,824 --> 00:33:14,199
Who else is as entertaining
as me so far?

520
00:33:14,907 --> 00:33:16,574
The Constellations

521
00:33:16,615 --> 00:33:19,115
must be so curious
what I'll do next.

522
00:33:19,907 --> 00:33:21,657
But if you kill me now...

523
00:33:21,699 --> 00:33:22,824
Could you handle the blowback?

524
00:33:22,865 --> 00:33:25,032
Uh... But how is it possible

525
00:33:25,074 --> 00:33:26,907
that you know all of this?

526
00:33:26,949 --> 00:33:29,449
Close your channel for a sec.
Let's talk.

527
00:33:31,199 --> 00:33:35,782
Oh, wow. Constellations,
let take a quick ad break, okay?

528
00:33:39,990 --> 00:33:42,740
Hmm. Now speak.

529
00:33:42,782 --> 00:33:45,782
How can an ordinary human
know about star streams?

530
00:33:45,824 --> 00:33:48,699
Oh, shit. That hurts.

531
00:33:48,740 --> 00:33:50,365
Star steams are not important.

532
00:33:50,407 --> 00:33:52,365
Uh, what?
You told me to close it!

533
00:33:52,407 --> 00:33:54,574
Bihyung,

534
00:33:54,615 --> 00:33:56,032
you need to think
about this, huh?

535
00:33:56,074 --> 00:33:57,324
- Hmm?
- How long you've been

536
00:33:57,365 --> 00:33:59,699
a panhandle to some
lowly ninth-grade Dokkaebi?

537
00:33:59,740 --> 00:34:01,740
Huh? What are you saying?

538
00:34:01,782 --> 00:34:04,240
What does a Dokkaebi
do anyway?

539
00:34:04,282 --> 00:34:06,532
Let Constellations
into your channel

540
00:34:06,574 --> 00:34:09,990
and show them random stories
and scenarios with humans?

541
00:34:10,032 --> 00:34:13,032
Hopefully get enough donations
to be a first-grade Dokkaebi.

542
00:34:13,074 --> 00:34:15,199
But I guarantee you,

543
00:34:15,240 --> 00:34:18,615
my story will be better
than you can ever imagine.

544
00:34:18,657 --> 00:34:20,240
Hmm...

545
00:34:20,282 --> 00:34:22,449
Sign an exclusive
contract with me.

546
00:34:23,782 --> 00:34:25,490
And you'll be the Dokkaebi king.

547
00:34:25,532 --> 00:34:27,282
Wow!

548
00:34:29,449 --> 00:34:32,032
You poor human.
You're overreaching.

549
00:34:32,074 --> 00:34:35,240
Why sign a contract with someone
who's about to die?

550
00:34:35,282 --> 00:34:36,532
Why do you think
Constellations

551
00:34:36,574 --> 00:34:38,324
watch the streams, huh?

552
00:34:38,365 --> 00:34:39,740
Well, it's very amusing

553
00:34:39,782 --> 00:34:41,990
watching puny humans
struggle to survive.

554
00:34:42,032 --> 00:34:43,782
That's why they donate, too.

555
00:34:43,824 --> 00:34:45,824
Of course.

556
00:34:45,865 --> 00:34:47,990
Well, then suppose
we do sign a contract.

557
00:34:48,032 --> 00:34:51,240
<i>In the subway I used ants
to clear the scenario</i>

558
00:34:51,282 --> 00:34:54,199
<i>and I fought Kim Namwoon
using my skills.</i>

559
00:34:54,240 --> 00:34:56,074
Then I was eaten by
an Ichthyosaur,

560
00:34:56,115 --> 00:34:57,824
but if I escape
and keep clearing

561
00:34:57,865 --> 00:34:59,365
every scenario once I get out,

562
00:34:59,407 --> 00:35:02,657
how many donations do you think
our channel will get, huh?

563
00:35:02,699 --> 00:35:05,949
How can I be sure
you can do all that?

564
00:35:05,990 --> 00:35:09,074
Why don't you go see how many
donations you have now?

565
00:35:09,115 --> 00:35:10,365
Hmm?

566
00:35:10,407 --> 00:35:12,407
Oh...

567
00:35:14,949 --> 00:35:17,324
Whoa, look at all this.
How many zeros!

568
00:35:17,365 --> 00:35:19,074
I can't believe this!

569
00:35:20,782 --> 00:35:22,282
Okay, let's sign a contract!

570
00:35:22,324 --> 00:35:23,282
<i>Exclusive Contract for Partnership</i>

571
00:35:23,324 --> 00:35:25,324
We split the profits 50:50, okay?

572
00:35:25,365 --> 00:35:26,824
Hmm.

573
00:35:39,407 --> 00:35:42,574
Oh. It's starting. Okay.

574
00:35:43,282 --> 00:35:45,782
Constellations,
the Ichthyosaur stomach acid

575
00:35:45,824 --> 00:35:46,824
has started to flow.

576
00:35:46,865 --> 00:35:48,157
How will our human escape this?

577
00:35:48,199 --> 00:35:50,615
<i>Bihyung.
Open the Dokkaebi shop, please.</i>

578
00:35:50,990 --> 00:35:52,699
The Dokkaebi shop?

579
00:35:52,740 --> 00:35:55,282
How on earth do you
know all of this?

580
00:36:06,407 --> 00:36:08,699
The human has
purchased an item.

581
00:36:08,740 --> 00:36:11,157
Let's see what he plans
to do with it.

582
00:36:19,865 --> 00:36:22,240
<i>: Yoo Junghyuk
was trapped in an Ichthyosaur</i>

583
00:36:22,282 --> 00:36:23,699
<i>stomach once, too.</i>

584
00:36:24,532 --> 00:36:27,490
<i>If you block all its stomach
acid ducts with thorns,</i>

585
00:36:27,532 --> 00:36:29,032
<i>it'll die.</i>

586
00:36:29,949 --> 00:36:31,990
<i>But the problem is...</i>

587
00:36:32,615 --> 00:36:34,449
<i>there are so many of them.</i>

588
00:36:45,157 --> 00:36:48,074
<i>In a few days, you'll die
fighting the fire dragon.</i>

589
00:36:48,115 --> 00:36:50,115
<i>In Chungmuro station.</i>

590
00:36:50,157 --> 00:36:51,657
<i>Even if you regress,
it'll take a long time</i>

591
00:36:51,699 --> 00:36:53,365
<i>to clear this scenario.</i>

592
00:36:53,407 --> 00:36:56,615
<i>But if we go together,
you can defeat the fire dragon.</i>

593
00:37:16,324 --> 00:37:18,407
<i>This scenario's a test
of endurance.</i>

594
00:37:20,990 --> 00:37:22,907
<i>The last one.</i>

595
00:37:36,365 --> 00:37:38,740
<i>: The hidden
scenario has been cleared.</i>

596
00:37:38,782 --> 00:37:40,865
<i>9,000 coins have been awarded.</i>

597
00:37:44,032 --> 00:37:46,324
Huh? Wait. Is it true?

598
00:37:46,365 --> 00:37:49,449
Dokja, did you really defeat
the Ichthyosaur?

599
00:37:49,490 --> 00:37:51,282
- Amazing!
- Get out of the way. Move!

600
00:37:51,324 --> 00:37:52,282
Oh.

601
00:38:09,824 --> 00:38:12,657
Wait.
That's the Ichthyosaur Nucleus.

602
00:38:12,699 --> 00:38:15,032
How did you know where it was?

603
00:38:15,074 --> 00:38:16,907
Put this in
the Dokkaebi shop auction.

604
00:38:16,949 --> 00:38:19,199
- Ah...
- Not to sell.

605
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:20,949
I want a one-to-one trade.

606
00:38:20,990 --> 00:38:23,490
And I'll only trade it
for Ether of Faith.

607
00:38:23,532 --> 00:38:25,657
Put up a notification window
when there's an offer.

608
00:38:25,699 --> 00:38:26,865
Dokja,

609
00:38:26,907 --> 00:38:28,907
this is very impressive.
I must say,

610
00:38:28,949 --> 00:38:31,074
killing the mighty
Ichthyosaur is one thing,

611
00:38:31,115 --> 00:38:33,490
but knowing exactly
where to find its nucleus

612
00:38:33,532 --> 00:38:36,199
and wanting to trade
for Ether of Faith...

613
00:38:36,240 --> 00:38:39,490
Ether of Faith
is so incredibly rare,

614
00:38:39,532 --> 00:38:42,740
I doubt anyone in the early
scenario will have it.

615
00:38:42,782 --> 00:38:44,824
Yeah? We'll let's try
and get it.

616
00:38:44,865 --> 00:38:46,449
Soon as we can.

617
00:38:46,490 --> 00:38:48,490
And when I call you,
come right away.

618
00:38:48,532 --> 00:38:50,865
And open the Dokkaebi shop
when I need it.

619
00:38:50,907 --> 00:38:53,532
- Okay?
- I'll do my best, Dokja.

620
00:38:53,574 --> 00:38:55,657
And it's nothing big,
but here's a gift

621
00:38:55,699 --> 00:38:57,324
to celebrate our contract.

622
00:38:57,365 --> 00:38:59,699
You'll need it when you go out.

623
00:39:00,740 --> 00:39:03,199
{\an8}Huh.
A starter pack.

624
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:05,282
Nice.

625
00:39:26,782 --> 00:39:29,199
<i>: The Constellation
Hunter of the Dark Moon</i>

626
00:39:29,240 --> 00:39:30,824
<i>admires your endurance,</i>

627
00:39:30,865 --> 00:39:33,490
<i>and wishes to sponsor you
and join you on your journey.</i>

628
00:39:33,532 --> 00:39:35,532
<i>The Constellation Bringer
of Dark Light</i>

629
00:39:35,574 --> 00:39:37,574
<i>wishes to sponsor you
and join you on your journey.</i>

630
00:39:37,615 --> 00:39:39,157
<i>: Constellations,</i>

631
00:39:39,199 --> 00:39:41,365
<i>you're really enjoying this,
aren't you?</i>

632
00:39:52,740 --> 00:39:55,199
{\an8}Hey, Bihyeong, turn off
all notifications

633
00:39:55,240 --> 00:39:56,574
{\an8}related to Constellations.

634
00:39:56,615 --> 00:39:59,282
{\an8}Yes, sir. But where
are you going now?

635
00:39:59,324 --> 00:40:02,365
Geumho Station, I need
to meet someone there.

636
00:40:02,407 --> 00:40:04,615
Are you referring
to the tall fellow?

637
00:40:04,657 --> 00:40:07,074
I wouldn't do that,
he's got many items,

638
00:40:07,115 --> 00:40:09,115
and his level far exceeds
your own.

639
00:40:09,157 --> 00:40:12,657
We just signed a contract,
what'll I do if you die?

640
00:40:12,699 --> 00:40:14,074
I'm hungry.

641
00:40:37,740 --> 00:40:40,324
Hey, hey, hey.

642
00:40:45,032 --> 00:40:47,990
Hey. Can you hear me?
I need you to wake up.

643
00:40:48,865 --> 00:40:50,699
You good? Can you stand up?

644
00:40:59,657 --> 00:41:01,199
Ahh!

645
00:41:01,782 --> 00:41:03,324
Did you say Exit One?

646
00:41:06,990 --> 00:41:08,324
Wait!

647
00:41:11,657 --> 00:41:13,240
Wait! Please wait!

648
00:41:42,074 --> 00:41:44,199
Hey, are you okay?

649
00:41:45,282 --> 00:41:47,074
- Over there!
- What's going on?

650
00:41:48,240 --> 00:41:49,907
- Can it be?
- Yeah, look, see. Over there!

651
00:41:49,949 --> 00:41:53,532
Jeong Heewon?
Are you really alive?

652
00:41:53,574 --> 00:41:54,907
<i>: Jeong Heewon?</i>

653
00:41:54,949 --> 00:41:56,657
I thought for sure
you were done for.

654
00:41:56,699 --> 00:41:58,365
I'm gonna kill that asshole!

655
00:41:58,407 --> 00:42:01,032
Er, just one question.

656
00:42:01,074 --> 00:42:04,449
Why did you bother dragging
her all the way back in here,

657
00:42:04,490 --> 00:42:07,782
when you know damn well
we already finished with her?

658
00:42:08,490 --> 00:42:10,365
Come on, don't be a nuisance!

659
00:42:10,407 --> 00:42:11,740
<i>: This chapter
in the novel</i>

660
00:42:11,782 --> 00:42:13,657
<i>was particularly boring.</i>

661
00:42:15,032 --> 00:42:17,615
<i>The characters
were such stereotypes.</i>

662
00:42:17,657 --> 00:42:18,990
Bang Cheolsu?

663
00:42:19,032 --> 00:42:22,074
Excuse me? You know who I am?

664
00:42:22,115 --> 00:42:25,157
Well, let's do it.

665
00:42:25,199 --> 00:42:27,240
<i>Spend 1,500 coins on Strength.</i>

666
00:42:27,282 --> 00:42:29,740
<i>: 1,500 coins
spent on Strength.</i>

667
00:42:34,824 --> 00:42:38,032
Holy crap, he's using skills?

668
00:42:38,824 --> 00:42:40,824
Hey man, you should've
just said so!

669
00:42:40,865 --> 00:42:43,407
<i>: Bang Cheolsu
is supported by his sponsor,</i>

670
00:42:43,449 --> 00:42:44,824
<i>Monarch of the Small Fries.</i>

671
00:42:44,865 --> 00:42:48,157
<i>Why would he choose
such a shitty sponsor?</i>

672
00:42:48,199 --> 00:42:52,157
<i>Right, chest, right.
This guy's so predictable.</i>

673
00:42:56,782 --> 00:42:58,740
Argh, ugh!

674
00:42:58,782 --> 00:43:00,740
- Boss, you okay?
- What are you waiting for?

675
00:43:00,782 --> 00:43:02,824
- Kill him! Now!
- You okay, boss?

676
00:43:06,865 --> 00:43:08,615
Bang Cheolsu!

677
00:43:10,782 --> 00:43:13,240
What is going on down here?

678
00:43:13,282 --> 00:43:16,865
Ah, shit! Come on, let's go.

679
00:43:25,115 --> 00:43:26,865
Oh.

680
00:43:26,907 --> 00:43:30,157
<i>Wait, who the hell is this guy?</i>

681
00:43:32,949 --> 00:43:35,782
Huh? Dokja!

682
00:43:35,824 --> 00:43:37,199
Ah!

683
00:43:40,990 --> 00:43:42,532
Ah...

684
00:43:45,824 --> 00:43:47,657
The people are saying
the congressman

685
00:43:47,699 --> 00:43:51,074
is the only reason
they've all survived down here.

686
00:43:51,115 --> 00:43:53,074
He's been able to persuade
the high-level people

687
00:43:53,115 --> 00:43:55,074
to provide, like,
go out and hunt,

688
00:43:55,115 --> 00:43:57,240
then share it
with the residents.

689
00:43:57,282 --> 00:43:59,949
All done, it should heal
pretty quickly.

690
00:44:02,532 --> 00:44:05,365
Gilyeong, I told you
to please stop doing that!

691
00:44:05,407 --> 00:44:07,199
Why? They're my friends.

692
00:44:07,240 --> 00:44:10,074
Oh, he's been acting weird
since that day on the train.

693
00:44:10,115 --> 00:44:13,240
He says he can talk to bugs when
he puts his hands up like that.

694
00:44:13,282 --> 00:44:15,865
I'm not weird,
I just like doing this.

695
00:44:16,990 --> 00:44:18,407
Hmph!

696
00:44:18,449 --> 00:44:20,740
Mr. Dokja.

697
00:44:20,782 --> 00:44:23,240
Why did that man
on the bridge

698
00:44:23,282 --> 00:44:25,282
just let you fall like that?

699
00:44:25,324 --> 00:44:26,699
What?

700
00:44:27,324 --> 00:44:29,615
Heh, oh him.

701
00:44:29,657 --> 00:44:31,365
I've known him since
I was in school.

702
00:44:31,407 --> 00:44:35,115
He's never been the easiest guy
to get along with, you know?

703
00:44:35,157 --> 00:44:36,699
Didn't he cause
a scene here too?

704
00:44:36,740 --> 00:44:39,490
No, he hasn't
been here at all.

705
00:44:40,824 --> 00:44:42,532
A-are you sure?

706
00:44:42,574 --> 00:44:45,365
He crossed the bridge,
and even when the gas came out,

707
00:44:45,407 --> 00:44:47,615
he just walked away to Namsan.

708
00:44:47,657 --> 00:44:50,990
<i>: Yoo Junghyuk didn't
come to Geumho Station?</i>

709
00:44:51,032 --> 00:44:53,157
<i>That doesn't make sense.</i>

710
00:44:53,199 --> 00:44:57,365
Hold on, that means you haven't
cleared the scenario, have you?

711
00:44:57,407 --> 00:44:59,449
A group of people
went into the tunnel

712
00:44:59,490 --> 00:45:02,699
to try and clear it,
but no one came back.

713
00:45:04,199 --> 00:45:06,532
<i>Damn, if we can't clear it,</i>

714
00:45:06,574 --> 00:45:09,240
<i>we can't pass the barrier
and get to Chungmuro.</i>

715
00:45:09,282 --> 00:45:11,907
<i>But that isn't
what happens in the novel.</i>

716
00:45:11,949 --> 00:45:14,907
Alright everyone, listen up.

717
00:45:15,449 --> 00:45:18,615
The survival fee payment
is due in three hours.

718
00:45:18,657 --> 00:45:21,365
Search party'll leave
in five minutes,

719
00:45:21,407 --> 00:45:22,907
so make sure you're ready.

720
00:45:22,949 --> 00:45:25,324
We let the elderly stay behind,

721
00:45:25,365 --> 00:45:28,282
but every able-bodied man
is required to come with us.

722
00:45:28,324 --> 00:45:30,990
<i>The Geumho Station scenario
exacts a survival fee</i>

723
00:45:31,032 --> 00:45:34,324
<i>on all residents, until
all the monsters are defeated.</i>

724
00:45:34,365 --> 00:45:36,949
<i>One hundred coins per day.</i>

725
00:45:36,990 --> 00:45:38,574
<i>Residents who couldn't afford
the fee</i>

726
00:45:38,615 --> 00:45:40,657
<i>went out on dangerous hunts.</i>

727
00:45:41,907 --> 00:45:44,074
<i>And those who couldn't
make the payments...</i>

728
00:45:45,615 --> 00:45:47,990
<i>...would die on the spot.</i>

729
00:45:49,490 --> 00:45:51,074
Hey, you!

730
00:45:52,532 --> 00:45:54,282
You, new guy!

731
00:45:57,865 --> 00:46:00,699
They say that you took
all the coins for yourself,

732
00:46:00,740 --> 00:46:02,240
is that true?

733
00:46:02,282 --> 00:46:03,949
- What?
- You earned coins

734
00:46:03,990 --> 00:46:06,657
by hunting monsters
in this district, didn't you?

735
00:46:06,699 --> 00:46:08,699
Then share the coins
with the rest of us!

736
00:46:08,740 --> 00:46:11,449
What, you were just gonna keep
your mouth shut and not tell us?

737
00:46:11,490 --> 00:46:12,907
Give the coins
to the congressman,

738
00:46:12,949 --> 00:46:14,532
so they can be shared
with everyone!

739
00:46:14,574 --> 00:46:16,074
He thinks
he's the only one suffering!

740
00:46:16,115 --> 00:46:17,199
- Yeah, exactly!
- It's true!

741
00:46:17,240 --> 00:46:18,615
No, give it to us!

742
00:46:18,657 --> 00:46:19,782
Look, I think

743
00:46:19,824 --> 00:46:21,990
there's been some sort
of misunderstanding.

744
00:46:22,032 --> 00:46:23,365
I've never gone out hunting.

745
00:46:23,407 --> 00:46:25,115
Don't lie,
we know you have, huh!

746
00:46:25,157 --> 00:46:26,824
- I don't believe this guy!
- Come on, we know

747
00:46:26,865 --> 00:46:28,657
the only reason you fight
so well is because

748
00:46:28,699 --> 00:46:30,115
you earned those coins
while hunting!

749
00:46:30,157 --> 00:46:32,865
Er, no, really,
I've never been hunting.

750
00:46:32,907 --> 00:46:36,449
And, even if I had,
then those coins would be mine.

751
00:46:36,490 --> 00:46:40,574
He just doesn't understand!
Listen, this is how it works.

752
00:46:40,615 --> 00:46:42,324
The only reason we've survived
this long

753
00:46:42,365 --> 00:46:44,699
is by pooling our strength
and working together.

754
00:46:46,240 --> 00:46:51,407
Oh, right. You must have.

755
00:46:51,449 --> 00:46:52,990
But...

756
00:46:53,032 --> 00:46:55,657
who exactly told you
I have all these coins?

757
00:46:55,699 --> 00:46:58,115
Does that really even matter?

758
00:46:58,157 --> 00:47:01,032
Please, just go to the office
and turn them in.

759
00:47:01,074 --> 00:47:02,282
We're all really desperate here.

760
00:47:02,324 --> 00:47:03,949
So then, you should just tell
me.

761
00:47:03,990 --> 00:47:05,115
And if you do,

762
00:47:05,157 --> 00:47:07,199
I'll give you each
100 coins. Huh?

763
00:47:08,532 --> 00:47:11,407
Who told you? Bang Cheolsu?

764
00:47:11,449 --> 00:47:13,074
I told them.

765
00:47:17,324 --> 00:47:20,115
When I saw how proficient
you were fighting that gang,

766
00:47:20,157 --> 00:47:22,865
I just knew. Usually,
those with a lot of coins

767
00:47:22,907 --> 00:47:25,324
are least willing to help
those in need.

768
00:47:25,365 --> 00:47:27,615
I was hoping you'd understand
how dire our situation

769
00:47:27,657 --> 00:47:30,990
is down here,
but with us being so desperate,

770
00:47:31,032 --> 00:47:33,615
we may have been a bit rude.

771
00:47:33,657 --> 00:47:35,657
If we offended you at all,
I apologize.

772
00:47:35,699 --> 00:47:38,699
No, no please, it's okay.
I-I'm not offended.

773
00:47:40,032 --> 00:47:42,574
Kim Dokja,

774
00:47:42,615 --> 00:47:45,657
20 people can't afford
the fee today.

775
00:47:45,699 --> 00:47:49,615
I want to keep everyone alive
by any means necessary.

776
00:47:49,657 --> 00:47:52,782
Please help us,
I'm begging you, sir.

777
00:47:54,907 --> 00:47:56,824
<i>: Wait,</i>

778
00:47:56,865 --> 00:47:58,865
<i>I remember now.</i>

779
00:47:58,907 --> 00:48:00,865
<i>I know who this man is.</i>

780
00:48:01,907 --> 00:48:03,740
You want my coins?

781
00:48:04,990 --> 00:48:06,949
Well, that's not gonna happen.

782
00:48:10,824 --> 00:48:13,699
You really don't care if 20
of these people die today?

783
00:48:13,740 --> 00:48:16,324
Even if they live today,
there's still tomorrow.

784
00:48:16,365 --> 00:48:17,824
Let's deal with today first!

785
00:48:17,865 --> 00:48:19,657
How can you just stand there
and not help?

786
00:48:21,449 --> 00:48:23,574
Alright, that's enough.

787
00:48:23,615 --> 00:48:25,907
Everyone, please stay calm.

788
00:48:32,324 --> 00:48:34,032
What's wrong with you?

789
00:48:35,490 --> 00:48:37,990
I thought you were
a good person, Mr. Kim.

790
00:48:39,824 --> 00:48:42,657
But I guess I read you
all wrong.

791
00:48:45,907 --> 00:48:48,907
Alright. I'll help you.

792
00:48:52,240 --> 00:48:53,865
But even if I give you
the coins,

793
00:48:53,907 --> 00:48:55,907
you'll still need more tomorrow.

794
00:48:55,949 --> 00:48:58,615
So instead,

795
00:48:58,657 --> 00:49:00,115
"Pass Through the Tunnel

796
00:49:00,157 --> 00:49:02,324
and Neutralize All
the Monsters Within It."

797
00:49:03,282 --> 00:49:08,282
I'll clear the scenario
for you. Okay?

798
00:49:09,699 --> 00:49:12,449
<i>Cheon Inho of Geumho Station.</i>

799
00:49:12,490 --> 00:49:16,490
<i>He sold himself
to the Constellations,</i>

800
00:49:16,532 --> 00:49:20,240
<i>and gave up his humanity
to become a monster.</i>

801
00:49:21,407 --> 00:49:24,115
Ant eggs?
Instead of human beings?

802
00:49:24,157 --> 00:49:28,282
Uh, that shouldn't be allowed,
should it? I mean, ah, ow...

803
00:49:28,324 --> 00:49:30,532
If a man like you
was beaten by him,

804
00:49:30,574 --> 00:49:33,449
the rumors must be true.

805
00:49:33,490 --> 00:49:35,157
Kim Dokja has the highest
abilities

806
00:49:35,199 --> 00:49:38,324
and most coins
in Geumho Station now by far.

807
00:49:38,365 --> 00:49:40,824
Well, if he's that strong,
he'll be able to clear

808
00:49:40,865 --> 00:49:42,657
the scenario, no problem!

809
00:49:45,865 --> 00:49:48,865
How many times
must I repeat myself to you?

810
00:49:48,907 --> 00:49:50,782
As long as I am here,
that scenario

811
00:49:50,824 --> 00:49:53,407
- will never be cleared!
- O-of course.

812
00:49:54,490 --> 00:49:56,407
You're right,
of course you're right.

813
00:49:56,449 --> 00:49:57,740
When you're right,
you're right.

814
00:49:59,865 --> 00:50:03,949
It's human nature for the weak
to bow down before the strong.

815
00:50:03,990 --> 00:50:06,074
A pathetic, meaningless
weakling like him,

816
00:50:06,115 --> 00:50:08,115
who suddenly gains strength,

817
00:50:08,157 --> 00:50:11,115
will run wild,
thinking he's a big shot.

818
00:50:12,657 --> 00:50:14,865
It's nothing
but reckless gallantry.

819
00:50:15,740 --> 00:50:18,074
This world is filled
with the decaying bodies

820
00:50:18,115 --> 00:50:20,574
- of nobodies like him.
- Well then, if he dies,

821
00:50:20,615 --> 00:50:22,657
we better make sure
we're the ones who collect

822
00:50:22,699 --> 00:50:25,740
all his coins. How much
do you think he really has?

823
00:50:25,782 --> 00:50:27,324
If the rumors are true,
it could be

824
00:50:27,365 --> 00:50:29,574
in the tens of thousands.

825
00:50:29,615 --> 00:50:32,240
Is that correct, Mr. Han?

826
00:50:33,657 --> 00:50:36,157
Yes. It's true, sorry.

827
00:50:36,199 --> 00:50:38,490
I saw it with my own eyes.

828
00:50:39,490 --> 00:50:40,740
Help yourself.

829
00:50:45,615 --> 00:50:48,407
I'm not going,
why would you go? We'll all die!

830
00:50:48,449 --> 00:50:50,282
We're not gonna die,
don't worry.

831
00:50:50,324 --> 00:50:51,657
I'll go, Mister!

832
00:50:51,699 --> 00:50:54,074
I had fun fighting
those monsters before.

833
00:50:54,115 --> 00:50:56,282
You think I'm gonna let you
fight any monsters?

834
00:50:56,324 --> 00:50:58,324
You're still in grade school.
No way!

835
00:50:58,365 --> 00:50:59,865
Mr. Dokja?

836
00:50:59,907 --> 00:51:01,782
If you have extra coins,
why do all this?

837
00:51:01,824 --> 00:51:03,240
Why not just share them
with everyone?

838
00:51:03,282 --> 00:51:04,615
Exactly, thank you!

839
00:51:04,657 --> 00:51:07,532
Why do we have to go through
all this trouble-- Oh!

840
00:51:07,574 --> 00:51:09,657
I mean, you, that is!

841
00:51:09,699 --> 00:51:12,449
Even if I shared the coins,
people would still die.

842
00:51:12,490 --> 00:51:14,407
If we want to stop people
from dying,

843
00:51:14,449 --> 00:51:16,407
we have to get to the root
of the problem.

844
00:51:17,407 --> 00:51:18,907
Isn't that so, Heewon?

845
00:51:21,074 --> 00:51:23,032
<i>In the novel,</i>

846
00:51:23,074 --> 00:51:25,032
<i>Heewon rebels against
Cheon Inho,</i>

847
00:51:25,074 --> 00:51:29,032
<i>loses her friends and dies
in the convenience store.</i>

848
00:51:29,074 --> 00:51:32,657
<i>Now, all she has left is rage.</i>

849
00:51:33,865 --> 00:51:37,865
You said the congressman
is behind all this, but how?

850
00:51:37,907 --> 00:51:39,657
When I found Heewon,

851
00:51:39,699 --> 00:51:41,949
it wasn't monsters
that attacked her.

852
00:51:41,990 --> 00:51:43,990
Bang Cheolsu's gang
is on his side, too.

853
00:51:44,032 --> 00:51:46,699
They recruit a search party
to go out looking for coins,

854
00:51:46,740 --> 00:51:48,907
and after hunting,
they quietly kill everyone.

855
00:51:48,949 --> 00:51:52,282
My friends died when we tried
to stop them once and for all.

856
00:51:52,324 --> 00:51:55,824
But, why? Why would
they kill those people?

857
00:51:55,865 --> 00:51:58,949
When you die, your coins
fall out for anyone to take.

858
00:52:00,115 --> 00:52:02,657
That bastard Cheon Inho
isn't really human.

859
00:52:06,240 --> 00:52:08,365
It's way too dark in here.

860
00:52:08,407 --> 00:52:10,740
How are we supposed to fight
if we can't see anything?

861
00:52:12,657 --> 00:52:15,490
Gilyeong,
can you give us a hand?

862
00:52:15,532 --> 00:52:17,490
Me? Can I?

863
00:52:17,532 --> 00:52:19,115
What are you talking about?

864
00:52:20,824 --> 00:52:23,449
That thing that
you thought of, show me.

865
00:52:26,157 --> 00:52:28,324
Hey Gilyeong, don't you dare
call cockroaches!

866
00:52:53,199 --> 00:52:54,699
Wow, Gilyeong!

867
00:52:59,490 --> 00:53:01,949
They told me
the monsters are coming.

868
00:53:08,407 --> 00:53:10,699
Make sure to use
your sponsors.

869
00:53:10,740 --> 00:53:12,949
You know how to increase your
abilities with coins, right?

870
00:53:12,990 --> 00:53:15,157
Spend all your coins
on strength and agility.

871
00:53:15,199 --> 00:53:18,157
All my coins? Shouldn't I save
some for the Survival Fee?

872
00:53:21,740 --> 00:53:24,032
Maintain this formation.

873
00:53:24,074 --> 00:53:26,449
Don't fight on your own,
we all need to help each other.

874
00:53:26,490 --> 00:53:28,865
Gilyeong,
keep the fireflies steady.

875
00:53:28,907 --> 00:53:31,157
But I wanna fight, too!

876
00:53:31,199 --> 00:53:33,157
Stay behind me.

877
00:53:37,990 --> 00:53:39,324
Argh!

878
00:53:42,532 --> 00:53:44,907
I got him!

879
00:54:07,740 --> 00:54:11,365
<i>Okay, if we follow that one,
we can get some new items.</i>

880
00:54:17,615 --> 00:54:20,157
Mister! If we go this way,
there's supposed to be

881
00:54:20,199 --> 00:54:23,199
really strong monsters, right?
The fireflies told me!

882
00:54:23,240 --> 00:54:25,074
Huh? I don't know.

883
00:54:25,115 --> 00:54:26,740
But you always seem
to know this stuff.

884
00:54:26,782 --> 00:54:29,032
You've been right
about everything.

885
00:54:29,074 --> 00:54:30,657
You're like a god
or something.

886
00:54:30,699 --> 00:54:32,615
Would I be doing this
if I were a god?

887
00:54:32,657 --> 00:54:35,324
<i>If there's any god here,
it's the author.</i>

888
00:54:40,032 --> 00:54:42,282
Sangah! Where are you?

889
00:54:42,324 --> 00:54:44,740
Dokja! Help!
I'm tied up in here!

890
00:54:44,782 --> 00:54:46,657
Ahh! What was that?

891
00:54:49,824 --> 00:54:51,574
<i>: Welcome.
You have now entered</i>

892
00:54:51,615 --> 00:54:53,282
<i>the Ground Rat's Shrine.</i>

893
00:54:53,324 --> 00:54:55,949
<i>Eliminate the Warden
of the Dark.</i>

894
00:55:04,032 --> 00:55:05,740
Alright, I guess
I'll go first.

895
00:55:28,990 --> 00:55:31,865
<i>Do I need an item
to defeat a Demon Species?</i>

896
00:55:31,907 --> 00:55:33,407
Mr. Dokja, I'm coming!

897
00:55:33,449 --> 00:55:35,657
Hyeonseong!
Don't! Wait! Stop!

898
00:55:49,532 --> 00:55:50,615
<i>What the...</i>

899
00:55:50,657 --> 00:55:51,490
Oh shit.

900
00:55:51,532 --> 00:55:52,449
<i>Can he do that?</i>

901
00:55:55,699 --> 00:55:56,824
<i>: The Warden
of the Dark</i>

902
00:55:56,865 --> 00:55:59,282
<i>has activated
an illusory prison.</i>

903
00:55:59,324 --> 00:56:01,074
Illusory prison?

904
00:56:03,865 --> 00:56:05,490
<i>: The illusory prison
traps the body</i>

905
00:56:05,532 --> 00:56:07,365
<i>and destroys the mind.</i>

906
00:56:07,407 --> 00:56:08,740
<i>If you're caught in it,</i>

907
00:56:08,782 --> 00:56:10,907
<i>you relive your worst memories
and die.</i>

908
00:56:13,199 --> 00:56:14,365
Run, Heewon!

909
00:56:36,032 --> 00:56:39,032
- What the hell was that?
- No time to explain!

910
00:56:39,074 --> 00:56:41,824
Gilyeong! No, wait! Stop!

911
00:56:59,740 --> 00:57:01,699
Over there, look!

912
00:57:11,490 --> 00:57:12,949
Ahh!

913
00:57:32,657 --> 00:57:34,990
Heewon! I need you
to buy me some time!

914
00:57:36,532 --> 00:57:39,240
- Hey, Bi-heyong, you watching?
- Of course, how can I help?

915
00:57:39,282 --> 00:57:41,740
Open the Dokkaebi shop,
White Star Pure Energy.

916
00:57:41,782 --> 00:57:45,532
But that's 50,000 coins,
you only have 49,000!

917
00:58:03,574 --> 00:58:05,907
Ahh!

918
00:58:15,407 --> 00:58:16,949
<i>: 50,000 coins paid.</i>

919
00:58:16,990 --> 00:58:19,615
<i>You have bought
White Star Pure Energy.</i>

920
00:58:23,907 --> 00:58:27,699
<i>Your weapon can now deliver
a one-time critical hit.</i>

921
00:58:48,615 --> 00:58:50,032
Hyeonseong!

922
00:59:24,074 --> 00:59:26,282
- Huh?
- Oh, he's awake!

923
00:59:26,324 --> 00:59:27,824
Hey, are you okay?

924
00:59:28,615 --> 00:59:30,115
I'm sorry.

925
00:59:30,157 --> 00:59:32,782
I must have fallen asleep
or something.

926
00:59:32,824 --> 00:59:34,115
Argh!

927
00:59:34,157 --> 00:59:35,615
Take it easy.

928
00:59:37,907 --> 00:59:40,699
You should get some rest.
You'll feel better, trust me.

929
00:59:41,657 --> 00:59:43,824
<i>The Hyeonseong in the novel
was so consumed</i>

930
00:59:43,865 --> 00:59:46,990
<i>by overwhelming guilt
for not saving someone</i>

931
00:59:47,032 --> 00:59:48,949
<i>that he was not able
to make full use</i>

932
00:59:48,990 --> 00:59:50,949
<i>of his abilities and potential.</i>

933
00:59:50,990 --> 00:59:54,865
<i>The Lee Hyeonseong here
is exactly the same.</i>

934
00:59:57,199 --> 01:00:00,282
Well, nice work, everyone.

935
01:00:00,324 --> 01:00:03,199
I think I spotted some treasure
chests further back there.

936
01:00:03,240 --> 01:00:05,115
Let's each go open one.

937
01:00:08,115 --> 01:00:10,074
Two swords for Heewon.

938
01:00:10,115 --> 01:00:12,782
An arm protector
for Hyeonseong.

939
01:00:12,824 --> 01:00:14,199
What about Gilyeong?

940
01:00:14,240 --> 01:00:15,532
When I wear this helmet,

941
01:00:15,574 --> 01:00:17,699
I can hear the insects
more clearly!

942
01:00:17,740 --> 01:00:20,782
Tada! Nice, huh?

943
01:00:20,824 --> 01:00:23,657
Apparently, it'll help me
fight better, too.

944
01:00:23,699 --> 01:00:26,657
Then, I guess
I'll open up mine now, too.

945
01:00:47,449 --> 01:00:49,490
Huh? But yours is broken!

946
01:00:49,532 --> 01:00:51,657
But you did the most,
why do you get something

947
01:00:51,699 --> 01:00:52,990
that doesn't work?

948
01:00:53,907 --> 01:00:57,907
It'll be useful somehow,
I'm sure. Let's go.

949
01:00:57,949 --> 01:01:00,157
<i>This is it, the Broken Faith.</i>

950
01:01:00,199 --> 01:01:02,574
<i>Now if I can just find
an Ether of Faith,</i>

951
01:01:02,615 --> 01:01:04,490
<i>the weapon will be complete.</i>

952
01:01:05,407 --> 01:01:07,615
Huh? What is this?

953
01:01:07,657 --> 01:01:10,990
Mister, I just found something
on the ground, what is it?

954
01:01:12,865 --> 01:01:14,532
Well, if you eat this,

955
01:01:14,574 --> 01:01:16,824
then those white hands
will come out,

956
01:01:16,865 --> 01:01:18,740
and you'll have scary dreams.

957
01:01:18,782 --> 01:01:21,282
So stay far away from it, okay?

958
01:01:21,324 --> 01:01:23,115
Alright, Mister.

959
01:01:23,782 --> 01:01:27,157
Dokja.

960
01:01:27,199 --> 01:01:29,782
How do you know all of this?

961
01:01:29,824 --> 01:01:31,740
What?

962
01:01:31,782 --> 01:01:33,949
Every step of the way,
you seem to know exactly

963
01:01:33,990 --> 01:01:36,115
what's coming
and where we need to go.

964
01:01:36,157 --> 01:01:39,490
It's like you've already
lived in this world.

965
01:01:39,532 --> 01:01:42,949
Okay, thank you!
I was thinking the same thing.

966
01:01:42,990 --> 01:01:44,949
What's going on with you,
Dokja?

967
01:01:46,074 --> 01:01:48,657
Okay, uh...

968
01:01:48,699 --> 01:01:52,782
I don't have any sponsors
or any real special skills.

969
01:01:52,824 --> 01:01:56,324
But I do seem to be able
to predict things

970
01:01:56,365 --> 01:01:58,865
before they happen,
like some sort of prophecy.

971
01:01:58,907 --> 01:02:01,324
Can you really see
what'll happen?

972
01:02:01,365 --> 01:02:02,907
Prophecy?

973
01:02:02,949 --> 01:02:05,949
Dokja,
that is so freaking cool!

974
01:02:05,990 --> 01:02:08,365
Then, do you know
what will happen to the world?

975
01:02:08,407 --> 01:02:10,407
Shouldn't you be able
to see that, too?

976
01:02:11,574 --> 01:02:13,907
Well, the world...

977
01:02:13,949 --> 01:02:16,157
can go back to how it was.

978
01:02:16,199 --> 01:02:17,782
Really?

979
01:02:17,824 --> 01:02:20,949
When?
Because I really wanna go home!

980
01:02:20,990 --> 01:02:23,949
Well, it's gonna
take some time.

981
01:02:23,990 --> 01:02:26,574
Then, tell us
what we have to do.

982
01:02:28,074 --> 01:02:31,740
We're gonna have to clear up
to the 99th scenario.

983
01:02:31,782 --> 01:02:35,199
The 99th?
Is that even possible?

984
01:02:35,949 --> 01:02:38,074
There is someone
who can do it.

985
01:02:38,115 --> 01:02:40,532
A hero who can clear
all scenarios.

986
01:02:40,574 --> 01:02:42,449
And save the whole world.

987
01:02:42,490 --> 01:02:46,157
And that's not... you?

988
01:02:49,865 --> 01:02:53,490
The two of you saw him
back on Dongho Bridge.

989
01:02:53,532 --> 01:02:55,282
Yoo Junghyuk.

990
01:03:10,032 --> 01:03:12,365
Wait, that guy?

991
01:03:12,407 --> 01:03:14,032
He was so good-looking!

992
01:03:14,074 --> 01:03:15,365
The problem is...

993
01:03:16,657 --> 01:03:19,574
tomorrow, he's gonna die
fighting a monster.

994
01:03:20,115 --> 01:03:22,532
But what happens if he dies?

995
01:03:22,574 --> 01:03:25,115
Then the world dies with him.

996
01:03:25,157 --> 01:03:27,657
It can never go back
to how it was.

997
01:03:28,824 --> 01:03:31,449
He'll be
at Chungmuro Station now.

998
01:03:31,490 --> 01:03:33,324
Once we finish clearing
this scenario,

999
01:03:33,365 --> 01:03:35,282
the barrier will be lifted,

1000
01:03:35,324 --> 01:03:37,282
and then I can go there
and help him.

1001
01:03:37,324 --> 01:03:38,740
I can try and save him somehow.

1002
01:03:38,782 --> 01:03:40,365
Wait!

1003
01:03:40,407 --> 01:03:43,365
Didn't we just bust our asses
clearing this scenario?

1004
01:03:43,407 --> 01:03:45,199
There's one monster left.

1005
01:03:47,699 --> 01:03:50,949
<i>: Ten minutes
until the Survival Fee payment.</i>

1006
01:03:50,990 --> 01:03:52,782
<i>Please have your payments
prepared.</i>

1007
01:03:52,824 --> 01:03:55,324
Hey, I just heard that people
in the search party

1008
01:03:55,365 --> 01:03:56,949
- are being killed for coins.
- Get off.

1009
01:03:56,990 --> 01:03:58,657
- My husband isn't back yet--
- Get off!

1010
01:03:58,699 --> 01:03:59,824
Damn, you're annoying!

1011
01:03:59,865 --> 01:04:02,282
Yeah, I killed your husband!
What about it?

1012
01:04:02,324 --> 01:04:03,907
- No! You didn't!
- Huh? What are you gonna

1013
01:04:03,949 --> 01:04:06,199
do about it?
Stupid annoying bitch.

1014
01:04:10,324 --> 01:04:13,032
I told you I'd kill you,
remember?

1015
01:04:13,907 --> 01:04:15,740
Sweet dreams!

1016
01:04:22,157 --> 01:04:24,199
Ms. Jeong Heewon!

1017
01:04:25,282 --> 01:04:27,407
If you really want to clear
the scenario,

1018
01:04:27,449 --> 01:04:29,990
you know what to do, so do it!

1019
01:04:30,032 --> 01:04:32,657
I mean, what is all this, huh?

1020
01:04:34,074 --> 01:04:36,032
That's why I'm here!

1021
01:04:36,074 --> 01:04:38,157
To kill the last monster
in the scenario.

1022
01:04:41,615 --> 01:04:43,865
Well, go on.

1023
01:04:43,907 --> 01:04:46,657
Kill them all
and take their coins.

1024
01:04:55,699 --> 01:04:57,115
<i>: In the novel,
Jeong Heewon</i>

1025
01:04:57,157 --> 01:04:58,449
<i>wasn't that famous,</i>

1026
01:04:58,490 --> 01:05:00,907
<i>and wasn't used much
in the story.</i>

1027
01:05:00,949 --> 01:05:04,490
<i>But maybe, that's why I rooted
for her more than anyone else.</i>

1028
01:05:05,449 --> 01:05:09,657
<i>Heewon, in this story,
you are the hero.</i>

1029
01:05:09,699 --> 01:05:12,490
<i>: The Constellation
Demonic Judge of Fire</i>

1030
01:05:12,532 --> 01:05:15,115
<i>approves the use of this skill.</i>

1031
01:05:16,949 --> 01:05:20,240
<i>Time of Judgment
has been activated.</i>

1032
01:05:42,865 --> 01:05:45,157
Ahh!

1033
01:06:00,449 --> 01:06:03,282
Argh!

1034
01:06:27,990 --> 01:06:31,407
Hey, wait! Miss!

1035
01:06:31,449 --> 01:06:33,157
Hold on.

1036
01:06:35,199 --> 01:06:37,824
You're not actually
gonna kill him, are you?

1037
01:06:37,865 --> 01:06:40,115
Maybe you don't know this,

1038
01:06:40,157 --> 01:06:42,449
but we don't clear
this scenario.

1039
01:06:42,490 --> 01:06:44,740
If we clear it,
the next one is even harder.

1040
01:06:44,782 --> 01:06:47,365
At a station nearby,
they cleared the scenario

1041
01:06:47,407 --> 01:06:50,115
and all got massacred
in the next one!

1042
01:06:50,157 --> 01:06:51,782
It's better and easier
for all of us to just

1043
01:06:51,824 --> 01:06:54,574
- pay the 100 coins every day.
- Hold on a second!

1044
01:06:54,615 --> 01:06:56,949
What the hell's the matter
with you people?

1045
01:06:56,990 --> 01:06:58,490
Why didn't you
tell us that before?

1046
01:06:58,532 --> 01:07:00,699
We just spent all our coins
fighting those monsters

1047
01:07:00,740 --> 01:07:02,324
to clear the scenario.

1048
01:07:02,365 --> 01:07:04,740
Well, every person who tried
to clear it before died,

1049
01:07:04,782 --> 01:07:09,157
so we assumed that
you all would just die too.

1050
01:07:09,199 --> 01:07:11,782
You saw when you die,
all your coins come out.

1051
01:07:11,824 --> 01:07:14,782
The congressman collected
and shared them all.

1052
01:07:14,824 --> 01:07:17,407
How were we supposed to know
you'd make it back?

1053
01:07:17,449 --> 01:07:18,824
Exactly.

1054
01:07:20,824 --> 01:07:22,740
<i>: Why'd this happen
to the world?</i>

1055
01:07:24,240 --> 01:07:28,282
Why are humans
the ones being punished?

1056
01:07:33,699 --> 01:07:36,365
<i>Is this what Yoo Junghyuk
was talking about?</i>

1057
01:07:37,990 --> 01:07:42,282
Kim Dokja!
I guess that means...

1058
01:07:43,865 --> 01:07:46,824
you don't have enough coins
to pay the survival fee!

1059
01:07:46,865 --> 01:07:49,490
<i>: Three minutes until
the Survival Fee payment.</i>

1060
01:07:49,532 --> 01:07:52,782
<i>Humans within this district,
prepare for payment.</i>

1061
01:08:14,157 --> 01:08:16,824
<i>One minute until
the Survival Fee payment.</i>

1062
01:08:16,864 --> 01:08:18,907
<i>Everyone prepare for payment.</i>

1063
01:08:18,949 --> 01:08:21,489
Hey, Heewon!
You need to catch him now!

1064
01:08:36,032 --> 01:08:38,282
Why are you so surprised?

1065
01:08:38,324 --> 01:08:39,824
It's the barrier!

1066
01:08:39,864 --> 01:08:41,657
You must have known you have
to clear the scenario

1067
01:08:41,699 --> 01:08:43,824
to pass it.

1068
01:08:43,864 --> 01:08:46,282
You killed all the most
monsters at Geumho Station,

1069
01:08:46,324 --> 01:08:48,114
except the most
important one.

1070
01:08:52,364 --> 01:08:53,699
Time's up!

1071
01:08:54,907 --> 01:08:56,907
- Wait!
- That reckless gallantry

1072
01:08:56,949 --> 01:08:59,032
of yours is always the problem,
isn't it?

1073
01:08:59,074 --> 01:09:01,449
And now, it's gonna get you
and your friends killed.

1074
01:09:06,907 --> 01:09:08,949
Take cover!

1075
01:09:10,574 --> 01:09:13,407
<i>: All monsters
have been neutralized.</i>

1076
01:09:13,449 --> 01:09:16,574
<i>The Daily Survival Fee
has now been lifted.</i>

1077
01:09:16,614 --> 01:09:19,657
<i>You have cleared
the main scenario.</i>

1078
01:09:22,032 --> 01:09:23,449
Who the hell is there?

1079
01:09:23,489 --> 01:09:26,864
Whoa, whoa!
What's with the attitude?

1080
01:09:26,907 --> 01:09:28,074
I just saved your butts,

1081
01:09:28,114 --> 01:09:29,864
shouldn't you all be
thanking me?

1082
01:09:36,949 --> 01:09:38,907
Since I killed him,

1083
01:09:38,949 --> 01:09:40,614
I'll just take all these.

1084
01:09:46,032 --> 01:09:48,407
Calm down, I won't hurt you.

1085
01:09:48,449 --> 01:09:50,114
I can tell you're just beggars.

1086
01:09:50,157 --> 01:09:53,157
Yes, well, thank you.

1087
01:09:53,199 --> 01:09:56,199
Hey, yeah, she looks kind
of terrifying, let's go.

1088
01:09:56,240 --> 01:09:58,907
Where are you going?
We need to clear the scenario.

1089
01:09:58,949 --> 01:10:01,157
Uh, but didn't we just
clear the scenario?

1090
01:10:01,199 --> 01:10:02,574
Thanks again, by the way.

1091
01:10:02,615 --> 01:10:04,740
Yeah, but that was
your scenario.

1092
01:10:04,782 --> 01:10:06,157
And you just stepped
into my district.

1093
01:10:06,199 --> 01:10:09,365
Ah, haha! Oh!

1094
01:10:09,407 --> 01:10:11,740
What's going on?
We're blocked again?

1095
01:10:11,782 --> 01:10:15,032
Yeah. And just so you know,

1096
01:10:15,074 --> 01:10:17,032
the scenario here isn't one
where you band together

1097
01:10:17,074 --> 01:10:18,740
and sing kumbaya.

1098
01:10:18,782 --> 01:10:20,407
It's everyone for themselves.

1099
01:10:22,282 --> 01:10:24,699
Are you guys really
just gonna stand there?

1100
01:10:24,740 --> 01:10:27,407
I'd suggest you start running.

1101
01:10:31,574 --> 01:10:33,074
<i>: Lee Jihye.</i>

1102
01:10:33,740 --> 01:10:35,574
{\an8}

1103
01:10:35,615 --> 01:10:38,407
<i>In the novel,
during the first scenario,</i>

1104
01:10:38,449 --> 01:10:40,115
<i>when everyone else
was panicking...</i>

1105
01:10:42,115 --> 01:10:44,157
Jihye, what are we gonna do?

1106
01:10:44,199 --> 01:10:45,699
<i>...Lee Jihye</i>

1107
01:10:47,824 --> 01:10:49,365
<i>survived on her own.</i>

1108
01:10:50,990 --> 01:10:53,365
<i>: Day Four of
the Chungmuro Station scenario</i>

1109
01:10:53,407 --> 01:10:56,615
<i>is starting. Ten minutes
before the monsters appear.</i>

1110
01:10:56,657 --> 01:10:58,615
<i>Green zones will be created.</i>

1111
01:10:58,657 --> 01:11:01,782
<i>Take refuge in a green zone
to survive.</i>

1112
01:11:01,824 --> 01:11:04,615
<i>Current survivors:
104 people.</i>

1113
01:11:04,657 --> 01:11:06,657
<i>Number of Green Zones for today:</i>

1114
01:11:06,699 --> 01:11:08,074
<i>52.</i>

1115
01:11:08,115 --> 01:11:09,990
<i>Take refuge in a Green Zone.</i>

1116
01:11:16,824 --> 01:11:18,740
Ten minutes left!

1117
01:11:18,782 --> 01:11:23,324
If you wanna live,
it's 750 coins per person.

1118
01:11:23,365 --> 01:11:27,990
It's safe in here, huh?
Ten minutes left!

1119
01:11:28,032 --> 01:11:30,865
There aren't many empty spaces!

1120
01:11:32,990 --> 01:11:35,824
Hello, sir. How much
in cash just for me?

1121
01:11:37,074 --> 01:11:39,365
The idiot said cash!

1122
01:11:39,407 --> 01:11:42,865
Look, buddy!
We don't take cash, huh?

1123
01:11:42,907 --> 01:11:44,282
You gotta bring us coins.

1124
01:11:44,324 --> 01:11:45,824
Look, I don't have any coins
on me,

1125
01:11:45,865 --> 01:11:47,782
but I'll give you as much cash
as you want.

1126
01:11:47,824 --> 01:11:49,157
- 20, 30 grand?
- Yeah, no, you gotta

1127
01:11:49,199 --> 01:11:50,115
get outta here.

1128
01:11:50,157 --> 01:11:51,324
Can't you read the sign, huh?

1129
01:11:51,365 --> 01:11:52,074
<i>1 night 1 person, 750 coins</i>

1130
01:11:52,115 --> 01:11:54,199
- Goddamnit.
- Please, just take this!

1131
01:11:55,115 --> 01:11:56,740
There's a hundred thousand
dollars in here.

1132
01:11:56,782 --> 01:11:58,532
- Save it!
- No, please, you gotta take it!

1133
01:11:58,574 --> 01:12:00,240
I said no! Now get outta here!

1134
01:12:00,282 --> 01:12:01,740
- Please, I swear--
- I said move it!

1135
01:12:01,782 --> 01:12:03,490
Hold on a second, hold on.

1136
01:12:05,532 --> 01:12:07,949
Where'd you get
a hundred thousand in cash?

1137
01:12:07,990 --> 01:12:10,199
I passed through
Myeongdong Station yesterday.

1138
01:12:10,240 --> 01:12:11,949
Some guy was offering
$100 per coin

1139
01:12:11,990 --> 01:12:14,032
to anyone who passed.

1140
01:12:14,074 --> 01:12:16,615
You never know when the world
might go back to normal, right?

1141
01:12:16,657 --> 01:12:18,282
So I exchanged it, just in case.

1142
01:12:18,324 --> 01:12:20,865
What's so funny?

1143
01:12:22,032 --> 01:12:24,699
That money's from my safe!

1144
01:12:24,740 --> 01:12:27,782
Idiots like him are the reason
I have so many coins!

1145
01:12:27,824 --> 01:12:29,615
The key to survival is adapting.

1146
01:12:29,657 --> 01:12:31,782
My God, you don't stand a chance

1147
01:12:31,824 --> 01:12:34,365
in this world, do you?
You sad, pathetic little man.

1148
01:12:34,407 --> 01:12:36,324
You'll be broke and dead!

1149
01:12:38,032 --> 01:12:39,782
<i>: Intruder detected.</i>

1150
01:12:50,074 --> 01:12:52,657
Tell me something,
why do the beggars fight so hard

1151
01:12:52,699 --> 01:12:54,449
to survive?

1152
01:12:54,490 --> 01:12:57,240
What do they wanna live for?
They have nothing!

1153
01:13:00,657 --> 01:13:04,157
Ah... We haven't even started!

1154
01:13:04,199 --> 01:13:06,907
Are we gonna have to fight
like this every day?

1155
01:13:06,949 --> 01:13:08,907
At midnight,

1156
01:13:08,949 --> 01:13:11,282
the monsters are all
gonna rush into the station.

1157
01:13:11,324 --> 01:13:13,574
You can live if you go inside
the green tiles.

1158
01:13:13,615 --> 01:13:15,157
We'll split up
and look for empty spots.

1159
01:13:15,199 --> 01:13:18,615
But listen, there may not be
room for all five of us.

1160
01:13:21,365 --> 01:13:24,532
If you find a green tile,
protect it at all costs.

1161
01:13:24,574 --> 01:13:27,824
That way, at least
one of us will live.

1162
01:13:27,865 --> 01:13:29,240
You got that?

1163
01:13:33,490 --> 01:13:36,949
<i>No spaces left
in Chungmuro Station.</i>

1164
01:13:36,990 --> 01:13:40,532
<i>If we wanna live, we have
to take someone else's spot.</i>

1165
01:13:41,490 --> 01:13:43,782
You're that prophet,
aren't you?

1166
01:13:45,990 --> 01:13:48,115
I heard about you from Master.

1167
01:13:48,157 --> 01:13:50,074
Since you've managed
to survive this long,

1168
01:13:50,115 --> 01:13:51,574
I guess it's working for you.

1169
01:13:52,574 --> 01:13:54,782
Yoo Junghyuk, where is he?

1170
01:13:57,282 --> 01:13:59,574
He got outta here already.

1171
01:13:59,615 --> 01:14:02,824
This scenario is nowhere near
his level, he's too powerful.

1172
01:14:04,365 --> 01:14:06,990
Why are you just standing there?

1173
01:14:07,032 --> 01:14:08,949
If you're really a prophet,
then you should know

1174
01:14:08,990 --> 01:14:11,824
where the bonus green zones
are gonna appear.

1175
01:14:14,449 --> 01:14:17,865
What? Too heroic
to just save yourself?

1176
01:14:18,449 --> 01:14:20,365
Master wanted me
to tell you this.

1177
01:14:20,407 --> 01:14:21,949
He'll take you up on your offer,

1178
01:14:21,990 --> 01:14:23,532
but you have
to leave the others,

1179
01:14:23,574 --> 01:14:26,282
and survive the night
all alone. Hmm.

1180
01:14:30,824 --> 01:14:33,449
What? You can't bear
to just save yourself?

1181
01:14:34,032 --> 01:14:36,074
But, but I just told you

1182
01:14:36,115 --> 01:14:38,949
what would happen
if you win, huh?

1183
01:14:38,990 --> 01:14:41,365
Hey, let's go.

1184
01:14:43,449 --> 01:14:45,199
Ho-ho!

1185
01:14:45,240 --> 01:14:48,657
What did I tell you, huh?
I told you they would do it!

1186
01:14:49,407 --> 01:14:51,824
You should give up.

1187
01:14:51,865 --> 01:14:53,824
Every time,
they always act like they won't,

1188
01:14:53,865 --> 01:14:55,324
but they do!

1189
01:14:55,365 --> 01:14:56,865
That way, at least...

1190
01:14:56,907 --> 01:14:58,782
<i>one of us gets to live.</i>

1191
01:15:01,115 --> 01:15:03,657
Get out of the way, it's mine!

1192
01:15:06,199 --> 01:15:07,615
I got it, I got it!

1193
01:15:14,199 --> 01:15:17,490
<i>6-1, 6-1.</i>

1194
01:15:18,532 --> 01:15:22,324
<i>Okay, so it's five tiles
back from the 6-1 mark.</i>

1195
01:15:25,115 --> 01:15:27,282
Dokja!

1196
01:15:29,240 --> 01:15:32,490
Dokja, we've looked everywhere,
there are no empty spots.

1197
01:15:32,532 --> 01:15:34,365
Gilyeong, over here!

1198
01:15:36,740 --> 01:15:39,532
Come on, you must know somewhere
else we can try and look.

1199
01:15:41,115 --> 01:15:43,699
Everyone listen up!

1200
01:15:45,657 --> 01:15:48,740
I'm Biryu, the Dokkaebi
in charge of this scenario.

1201
01:15:48,782 --> 01:15:50,615
You have less
than one minute left,

1202
01:15:50,657 --> 01:15:53,157
yet I'm not sure
I feel the urgency.

1203
01:15:53,199 --> 01:15:55,365
Are you starting to get tired?

1204
01:15:55,407 --> 01:15:58,449
Maybe I should just go ahead
and free the monsters right now.

1205
01:15:58,490 --> 01:16:00,865
Raise the tension
in here a little bit.

1206
01:16:00,907 --> 01:16:02,865
To those who don't have
a spot yet,

1207
01:16:02,907 --> 01:16:05,032
this is your last chance.

1208
01:16:05,074 --> 01:16:06,907
<i>: One minute warning.</i>

1209
01:16:06,949 --> 01:16:08,574
<i>Some green zones will vanish,</i>

1210
01:16:08,615 --> 01:16:11,157
<i>while other bonus green zones
will appear.</i>

1211
01:16:11,532 --> 01:16:12,574
What?

1212
01:16:22,032 --> 01:16:24,574
Dokja, come on.
We need to move right now!

1213
01:16:29,115 --> 01:16:33,157
Is... this prophecy as well?

1214
01:16:35,282 --> 01:16:36,949
It can't help in this scenario.

1215
01:16:38,824 --> 01:16:40,824
At least try for those spots.

1216
01:16:45,990 --> 01:16:49,865
If we push them out,
are those people just gonna die?

1217
01:16:51,490 --> 01:16:55,282
If you wanna live,
it can't be helped.

1218
01:16:56,490 --> 01:16:58,907
Can't we just fight them
like we did before?

1219
01:16:58,949 --> 01:17:00,449
How many monsters are there?

1220
01:17:00,490 --> 01:17:02,532
Hey! It doesn't work that way.

1221
01:17:02,574 --> 01:17:04,157
You'll die if you don't
find a zone!

1222
01:17:04,199 --> 01:17:07,532
<i>: The portal has now
opened, monsters are entering.</i>

1223
01:17:26,907 --> 01:17:29,240
You need to find a spot.

1224
01:17:29,282 --> 01:17:30,574
It's the only way
you'll make it!

1225
01:17:30,615 --> 01:17:31,990
What are you all doing?

1226
01:17:41,782 --> 01:17:43,615
It just can't end like this.

1227
01:17:46,699 --> 01:17:48,240
Wait up, wait!

1228
01:17:50,115 --> 01:17:53,490
Go towards the portal.
And, over there.

1229
01:17:53,532 --> 01:17:55,157
Isn't it more dangerous
down there?

1230
01:17:55,199 --> 01:17:58,449
All scenarios are designed
for max entertainment

1231
01:17:58,490 --> 01:18:00,490
for the Constellations.
If it's entertaining,

1232
01:18:00,532 --> 01:18:01,990
the rules can change.

1233
01:18:02,032 --> 01:18:04,532
Green Zones can appear
in the most dangerous places.

1234
01:18:04,574 --> 01:18:06,657
Hurry!

1235
01:18:09,074 --> 01:18:11,324
Dokja better be
sure about this!

1236
01:18:32,074 --> 01:18:33,865
I see one!

1237
01:18:34,365 --> 01:18:35,699
But wait, Mister...

1238
01:18:35,740 --> 01:18:37,074
Hey, kid. Please shut up.

1239
01:18:37,115 --> 01:18:39,157
You could've stayed
on your square.

1240
01:18:39,199 --> 01:18:41,949
- Why'd you come back?
- There's this novel I read

1241
01:18:41,990 --> 01:18:43,782
where only the hero survived.

1242
01:18:43,824 --> 01:18:46,490
But to be honest,
he was kind of a jerk.

1243
01:18:52,574 --> 01:18:54,157
<i>: Yoo Junghyuk?</i>

1244
01:19:04,032 --> 01:19:05,990
Hey, Yoo Junghyuk! Move over!

1245
01:19:06,032 --> 01:19:08,574
You don't need a Green Zone.
We do! Come on!

1246
01:19:09,657 --> 01:19:11,324
You wanna fight
the Dragon together?

1247
01:19:12,532 --> 01:19:15,032
Then this is your test.

1248
01:19:15,074 --> 01:19:16,657
Leave the boy and come on in.

1249
01:19:17,740 --> 01:19:19,324
Otherwise you both die.

1250
01:19:23,365 --> 01:19:25,407
Hyeonseong, grab on!

1251
01:19:39,449 --> 01:19:42,282
- Gilyeong, stay here.
- What about you?

1252
01:20:05,740 --> 01:20:07,074
<i>: If I eat this,</i>

1253
01:20:07,115 --> 01:20:09,699
<i>I'll be trapped
in the Illusory Prison.</i>

1254
01:20:21,657 --> 01:20:23,074
Had a feeling...

1255
01:20:33,449 --> 01:20:36,490
<i>: The Illusory
Prison has been activated.</i>

1256
01:20:49,240 --> 01:20:50,907
Whoa, he hit him!

1257
01:20:54,324 --> 01:20:56,199
Time's running out,
better hurry up!

1258
01:20:56,240 --> 01:20:57,657
Come on, let's go, boys!

1259
01:20:57,699 --> 01:20:59,324
I wanna see some action!

1260
01:21:42,032 --> 01:21:46,490
Whoa, stop! Stop!
Stop, hey, I'm sorry, okay?

1261
01:21:46,532 --> 01:21:47,865
I'm sorry!

1262
01:21:48,615 --> 01:21:50,490
Wow, Dokja,
you beat his ass!

1263
01:21:50,532 --> 01:21:52,157
<i>: Dear author,</i>

1264
01:21:52,199 --> 01:21:54,532
<i>Yoo Junghyuk once said,</i>

1265
01:21:54,574 --> 01:21:58,365
<i>"I can't help it if others
are sacrificed so I can live."</i>

1266
01:22:00,240 --> 01:22:02,824
<i>Is that the theme of the novel?</i>

1267
01:22:02,865 --> 01:22:05,532
<i>Because I can't accept that.</i>

1268
01:22:05,574 --> 01:22:10,199
<i>Sir, your novel is the worst.</i>

1269
01:22:20,407 --> 01:22:22,449
I'm sorry to tell
you that, yesterday,

1270
01:22:22,490 --> 01:22:24,824
<i>Minseop died.</i>

1271
01:22:24,865 --> 01:22:28,074
<i>We're still trying
to figure out all the details.</i>

1272
01:22:28,115 --> 01:22:29,740
<i>But for now, I know it's hard,</i>

1273
01:22:29,782 --> 01:22:32,199
<i>but try to focus
on today's mock exam.</i>

1274
01:22:51,699 --> 01:22:53,907
<i>: Author,</i>

1275
01:22:53,949 --> 01:22:58,574
<i>I once caused a friend's death
so that I could live.</i>

1276
01:23:00,365 --> 01:23:03,657
<i>In the novel, Yoo Junghyuk
seemed to be telling me</i>

1277
01:23:03,699 --> 01:23:05,657
<i>that it's not my fault.</i>

1278
01:23:07,490 --> 01:23:09,365
<i>That it couldn't be helped.</i>

1279
01:23:12,782 --> 01:23:15,282
<i>So I cheered for Yoo Junghyuk.</i>

1280
01:23:17,740 --> 01:23:20,740
<i>Until I read the ending
of the novel today.</i>

1281
01:23:22,865 --> 01:23:25,865
<i>I personally find
this ending terrifying.</i>

1282
01:23:28,324 --> 01:23:30,115
<i>And the reason is,</i>

1283
01:23:30,157 --> 01:23:33,990
<i>I'm scared it could also
happen to me.</i>

1284
01:23:38,157 --> 01:23:39,699
<i>Sir,</i>

1285
01:23:39,740 --> 01:23:42,282
<i>I wanted a different ending.</i>

1286
01:23:42,324 --> 01:23:45,199
<i>The ending I couldn't have,</i>

1287
01:23:45,240 --> 01:23:47,699
<i>where whatever sacrifice
it took,</i>

1288
01:23:47,740 --> 01:23:50,157
<i>the hero survived to the end</i>

1289
01:23:50,199 --> 01:23:52,282
<i>with his friends by his side.</i>

1290
01:23:52,324 --> 01:23:54,074
Don't be
ridiculous.

1291
01:23:54,115 --> 01:23:56,074
<i>: Yoo Junghyuk
has activated</i>

1292
01:23:56,115 --> 01:23:58,282
<i>the Dream Conversation skill.</i>

1293
01:23:59,365 --> 01:24:02,157
If that's what you wanted,
you would've fought that bully.

1294
01:24:04,115 --> 01:24:06,199
I know what you wanna do.

1295
01:24:07,282 --> 01:24:09,115
But humans aren't built
that way.

1296
01:24:11,324 --> 01:24:14,365
We aren't made to be
heroic and selfless.

1297
01:24:15,657 --> 01:24:18,032
I used to think like
you do now.

1298
01:24:19,032 --> 01:24:20,699
But after losing
too many friends

1299
01:24:20,740 --> 01:24:22,699
in this never-ending hellscape,

1300
01:24:24,074 --> 01:24:26,157
it just became easier
to fight alone.

1301
01:24:30,365 --> 01:24:31,782
But then...

1302
01:24:33,407 --> 01:24:35,282
what do we do now?

1303
01:24:36,365 --> 01:24:38,865
Why do you assume
you have to do something?

1304
01:24:40,574 --> 01:24:42,449
Remember, Dokja,
you're nothing.

1305
01:24:45,115 --> 01:24:46,532
His wounds
are too serious,

1306
01:24:46,574 --> 01:24:48,574
they're not getting better.

1307
01:24:53,490 --> 01:24:55,449
Dokja, are you okay?

1308
01:24:55,490 --> 01:24:57,074
I was worried you'd be out
of commission

1309
01:24:57,115 --> 01:24:58,740
for the rest of the day.

1310
01:25:00,407 --> 01:25:02,532
What happened to everyone?

1311
01:25:02,574 --> 01:25:05,365
- What's wrong with Hyeonseong?
-Mr. Dokja.

1312
01:25:05,407 --> 01:25:07,449
It's good to see you
up and about.

1313
01:25:07,490 --> 01:25:10,115
Hyeonseong pushed himself
too hard.

1314
01:25:10,157 --> 01:25:13,240
Sangah also strained herself
trying to heal him.

1315
01:25:13,282 --> 01:25:16,115
Are you sure you're really okay?

1316
01:25:16,157 --> 01:25:18,240
Yes, but, did we...

1317
01:25:19,490 --> 01:25:21,657
Did you fight the monsters
all night?

1318
01:25:22,490 --> 01:25:23,740
Because of me?

1319
01:25:25,449 --> 01:25:27,615
Oh, our time's up.

1320
01:25:27,657 --> 01:25:29,657
We need to go
to the next scenario.

1321
01:25:30,824 --> 01:25:33,699
<i>: My friends survived
outside the Green Zones.</i>

1322
01:25:33,740 --> 01:25:35,324
- Too tired.
- You need to wake up.

1323
01:25:35,365 --> 01:25:37,782
<i>- By all working together.</i>
-It's time to go.

1324
01:25:37,824 --> 01:25:41,949
<i>: Maybe the best way
to clear this scenario...</i>

1325
01:25:41,990 --> 01:25:44,282
Hyeonseong
and Gilyeong can't fight today.

1326
01:25:44,324 --> 01:25:46,574
You'll need to find two
Green Zones for them,

1327
01:25:46,615 --> 01:25:48,032
and we'll hold them off
out there.

1328
01:25:50,990 --> 01:25:52,365
But today...

1329
01:25:53,782 --> 01:25:55,782
Yoo Junghyuk dies.

1330
01:25:58,574 --> 01:26:01,324
On the last day of
the Chungmuro Station Scenario,

1331
01:26:01,365 --> 01:26:03,490
a Fire Dragon comes out.

1332
01:26:03,532 --> 01:26:06,157
Yoo Junghyuk will try
to fight it, and die.

1333
01:26:06,199 --> 01:26:08,824
But you told us if he dies,
then this world ends.

1334
01:26:08,865 --> 01:26:12,657
Well, to be clear, if the hero
who can save the world dies,

1335
01:26:12,699 --> 01:26:14,490
the world will be destroyed
within minutes.

1336
01:26:15,949 --> 01:26:17,490
In order to prevent that,

1337
01:26:17,532 --> 01:26:20,199
someone else needs
to fight the Fire Dragon.

1338
01:26:20,240 --> 01:26:21,949
Well, if that's us...

1339
01:26:23,490 --> 01:26:25,990
that would mean one of us
has to die, right?

1340
01:26:28,324 --> 01:26:29,657
I'll do it.

1341
01:26:30,490 --> 01:26:32,615
And besides,

1342
01:26:32,657 --> 01:26:35,365
I'd already be dead
if it weren't for Dokja.

1343
01:26:37,240 --> 01:26:39,782
Tell me what I have to do.

1344
01:26:40,532 --> 01:26:43,449
No.

1345
01:26:43,490 --> 01:26:46,282
There's something else
you need to do, Heewon.

1346
01:26:46,324 --> 01:26:49,157
- I have to do this.
- No, no, wait!

1347
01:26:49,199 --> 01:26:52,157
Yoo Junghyuk is at
a much higher level than you.

1348
01:26:52,199 --> 01:26:54,615
He's in a completely different
league than us.

1349
01:26:54,657 --> 01:26:56,657
If a person like him
can't kill it,

1350
01:26:56,699 --> 01:26:58,282
then where does that leave you?

1351
01:26:59,199 --> 01:27:02,199
You all protected me last night.

1352
01:27:03,407 --> 01:27:05,032
You saved my life.

1353
01:27:06,115 --> 01:27:11,115
And because of that,
now I see what I need to do.

1354
01:27:11,157 --> 01:27:14,782
<i>: Current number
of survivors, 57 people.</i>

1355
01:27:14,824 --> 01:27:16,865
<i>Number of Green Zones
for today...</i>

1356
01:27:21,282 --> 01:27:23,324
<i>We have an announcement.</i>

1357
01:27:23,365 --> 01:27:25,699
Everyone, listen up!

1358
01:27:25,740 --> 01:27:29,115
As you know, this scenario's
rule is everyone for themselves.

1359
01:27:29,157 --> 01:27:31,907
The concept is survive
on your own.

1360
01:27:31,949 --> 01:27:33,407
But last night,
some of you survived

1361
01:27:33,449 --> 01:27:35,365
outside of the Green Zones.

1362
01:27:35,407 --> 01:27:37,740
By helping each other.

1363
01:27:37,782 --> 01:27:41,449
Our dear Constellations
are very upset.

1364
01:27:41,490 --> 01:27:43,657
So today,
we'll be raising the difficulty.

1365
01:27:43,699 --> 01:27:46,740
<i>: Current survivors,
57 people.</i>

1366
01:27:46,782 --> 01:27:49,282
<i>Number of Green Zones
for today...</i>

1367
01:27:49,324 --> 01:27:50,282
<i>one.</i>

1368
01:27:50,324 --> 01:27:51,365
What?

1369
01:27:51,407 --> 01:27:52,449
You can't do that!

1370
01:27:52,490 --> 01:27:54,115
That's a death sentence
for all of us!

1371
01:27:54,157 --> 01:27:55,574
Quiet down!

1372
01:27:57,157 --> 01:27:58,990
Today, I'll be deciding
who is worthy

1373
01:27:59,032 --> 01:28:00,574
of the single Green Zone.

1374
01:28:00,615 --> 01:28:02,449
Who should get it, you ask?

1375
01:28:02,490 --> 01:28:06,324
The kindest human?
The most unfortunate human?

1376
01:28:06,365 --> 01:28:09,824
Or maybe the smartest human?

1377
01:28:09,865 --> 01:28:12,657
But I hear in your world,
the wealthiest reign.

1378
01:28:12,699 --> 01:28:14,990
Then let's do that.

1379
01:28:18,865 --> 01:28:21,365
<i>: A Green Zone
has appeared.</i>

1380
01:28:23,199 --> 01:28:26,740
If you want to live,
rise up and take this spot.

1381
01:28:26,782 --> 01:28:29,324
But even if you do,
there's still only one.

1382
01:28:36,365 --> 01:28:37,907
Hang on a minute.

1383
01:28:39,032 --> 01:28:41,490
Jihye! I need your help.

1384
01:28:41,532 --> 01:28:44,157
Why would I help you
when I can just take that space?

1385
01:28:45,449 --> 01:28:48,157
Work with us. Together,
we can do this, trust me.

1386
01:28:51,282 --> 01:28:52,865
If you'd just stayed
in that zone,

1387
01:28:52,907 --> 01:28:55,199
we wouldn't be in this mess.

1388
01:28:56,574 --> 01:28:57,907
Everyone's gonna die now

1389
01:28:57,949 --> 01:28:59,782
because you had to play
the hero.

1390
01:28:59,824 --> 01:29:02,199
And that's why I need
your help.

1391
01:29:02,240 --> 01:29:04,657
Listen, I have an idea.
You just need to help me--

1392
01:29:04,699 --> 01:29:06,240
I said no!

1393
01:29:06,282 --> 01:29:08,449
You saw who got the Green Zone.

1394
01:29:08,490 --> 01:29:10,240
In this world, it's always
the strong who survive,

1395
01:29:10,282 --> 01:29:11,865
and it always will be.

1396
01:29:11,907 --> 01:29:13,074
And I think that's great.

1397
01:29:13,115 --> 01:29:15,157
It's straightforward and fair.

1398
01:29:15,199 --> 01:29:18,157
If you don't wanna die,
then you just have to win.

1399
01:29:21,574 --> 01:29:23,824
Isn't it already enough?

1400
01:29:23,865 --> 01:29:26,115
That you killed your friend
to survive?

1401
01:29:27,615 --> 01:29:29,949
<i>Even as she took
her last breath,</i>

1402
01:29:29,990 --> 01:29:32,282
she didn't even lift
a finger to stop you.

1403
01:29:36,115 --> 01:29:37,574
I couldn't help it.

1404
01:29:40,949 --> 01:29:42,365
I couldn't
help it.

1405
01:29:49,949 --> 01:29:52,032
<i>: I know
you couldn't help it.</i>

1406
01:29:53,074 --> 01:29:54,365
<i>But you also know
what happened</i>

1407
01:29:54,407 --> 01:29:56,240
<i>when you tried to survive alone.</i>

1408
01:30:14,699 --> 01:30:16,282
Bihyeong, you there?

1409
01:30:16,324 --> 01:30:18,199
Dokja, wow!

1410
01:30:18,240 --> 01:30:19,282
Just like you told me,

1411
01:30:19,324 --> 01:30:21,407
our channel is absolutely
exploding!

1412
01:30:21,449 --> 01:30:23,449
The Constellations
love this story,

1413
01:30:23,490 --> 01:30:24,657
and donations are pouring in!

1414
01:30:24,699 --> 01:30:26,615
Let's cash in
those donations right now.

1415
01:30:26,657 --> 01:30:28,532
How much exactly?

1416
01:30:29,240 --> 01:30:30,740
All of it.

1417
01:30:41,449 --> 01:30:43,074
When I tell you,
shoot it all out.

1418
01:30:43,115 --> 01:30:45,157
Okay, hold on.
Let me convert it.

1419
01:30:47,449 --> 01:30:49,699
Hey, mister!

1420
01:30:49,740 --> 01:30:51,574
Yeah, you, Gong Pildoo!

1421
01:30:54,574 --> 01:30:56,324
Now what does this bum need?

1422
01:31:00,949 --> 01:31:04,074
Any chance you'll do
some work for me?

1423
01:31:04,115 --> 01:31:06,282
- What?
- I have an important job

1424
01:31:06,324 --> 01:31:08,907
for you. How much do you charge?

1425
01:31:08,949 --> 01:31:10,365
I thought you were just
some bum.

1426
01:31:10,407 --> 01:31:12,824
I didn't realize you were
also a kook.

1427
01:31:12,865 --> 01:31:14,574
How does a hundred thousand
coins sound?

1428
01:31:16,282 --> 01:31:18,907
That much?

1429
01:31:18,949 --> 01:31:20,532
Sure, if you really
have that much,

1430
01:31:20,574 --> 01:31:22,949
I'll do whatever stupid job
you want.

1431
01:31:22,990 --> 01:31:24,990
Now show me the coins.

1432
01:31:25,032 --> 01:31:25,990
Coming right up.

1433
01:31:26,032 --> 01:31:27,157
<i>Bihyeong, now.</i>

1434
01:31:27,199 --> 01:31:30,199
Here it comes, 113,000 coins!

1435
01:31:30,240 --> 01:31:32,615
<i>: The Green Zone
is being regenerated.</i>

1436
01:31:32,657 --> 01:31:34,490
My spot!

1437
01:31:52,699 --> 01:31:55,657
You crazy
son of a bitch! Stop!

1438
01:31:56,282 --> 01:31:58,490
Wait, you can't! No!

1439
01:31:58,532 --> 01:32:00,324
I'll shoot you!

1440
01:32:00,365 --> 01:32:01,824
Go ahead and shoot me then!

1441
01:32:06,199 --> 01:32:08,199
<i>I know you couldn't help it.</i>

1442
01:32:08,990 --> 01:32:12,407
<i>But you also know what happened
when you tried to survive alone.</i>

1443
01:32:15,532 --> 01:32:17,282
Get off me! Get off!

1444
01:32:41,990 --> 01:32:44,074
Hey, you!

1445
01:32:44,115 --> 01:32:46,449
What the hell did... damn.

1446
01:32:46,490 --> 01:32:48,657
That psychopath really
broke through it!

1447
01:32:48,699 --> 01:32:50,657
Out of my way.

1448
01:32:50,699 --> 01:32:53,657
Look at me, you bastard!
You destroyed my safe zone.

1449
01:32:53,699 --> 01:32:55,157
What're we gonna do now?

1450
01:32:55,199 --> 01:32:57,157
<i>: Monsters will enter
in one minute.</i>

1451
01:32:57,199 --> 01:32:58,657
<i>The portal is forming.</i>

1452
01:33:00,990 --> 01:33:02,907
- Listen to me!
- They're coming!

1453
01:33:02,949 --> 01:33:05,407
If those Green Zones
didn't exist,

1454
01:33:05,449 --> 01:33:07,782
we all would've
fought the monsters.

1455
01:33:07,824 --> 01:33:09,324
And maybe we'd have all
made it through.

1456
01:33:16,240 --> 01:33:19,615
<i>: 100,000 coins
have been transferred.</i>

1457
01:33:19,657 --> 01:33:21,782
- Where are you going?
- I paid you to do a job.

1458
01:33:21,824 --> 01:33:24,282
- Keep your word.
- But, but what do I do?

1459
01:33:24,324 --> 01:33:27,199
I don't want a single person
here to die.

1460
01:33:27,240 --> 01:33:29,115
I counted everyone!

1461
01:33:29,157 --> 01:33:30,990
Yeah, you need
to help all of us.

1462
01:33:31,032 --> 01:33:33,032
Right! Let us live too.

1463
01:33:33,074 --> 01:33:36,115
You owe it to us!

1464
01:33:37,490 --> 01:33:40,449
Hey, I won't charge you
for today.

1465
01:33:40,490 --> 01:33:42,449
So those who want
to fight, fight.

1466
01:33:42,490 --> 01:33:46,115
Those who can't,
come on to my land. Hurry!

1467
01:33:54,532 --> 01:33:57,199
Guess I'm gonna earn a shitload
of coins today.

1468
01:33:57,990 --> 01:34:00,157
<i>: The Constellation
Defense Master</i>

1469
01:34:00,199 --> 01:34:03,157
<i>has given emergency defense
to Gong Pildoo.</i>

1470
01:34:09,824 --> 01:34:11,699
Gilyeong and Hyeonseong
can't help us today.

1471
01:34:11,740 --> 01:34:13,282
We need to fight for them too.

1472
01:34:13,324 --> 01:34:16,157
Do me a favor,
don't die, you two!

1473
01:34:29,865 --> 01:34:32,324
Suck on that, you scum!

1474
01:35:42,157 --> 01:35:43,782
- Gong Pildoo!
- Die you little--

1475
01:35:43,824 --> 01:35:45,740
I'll take that one.
Keep blocking the entrance.

1476
01:35:45,782 --> 01:35:47,907
Go, quick!

1477
01:35:53,907 --> 01:35:56,324
Yoo Junghyuk! Wait!

1478
01:35:58,907 --> 01:36:01,157
If you fight, you'll die.
Let me do it.

1479
01:36:08,074 --> 01:36:09,157
With that sword?

1480
01:36:11,199 --> 01:36:12,907
What was it? Four days ago?

1481
01:36:12,949 --> 01:36:14,532
When you predicted I'd die?

1482
01:36:15,282 --> 01:36:17,115
Watch this.

1483
01:36:47,699 --> 01:36:49,740
<i>: There's a human
in this area</i>

1484
01:36:49,782 --> 01:36:51,782
<i>with abnormal abilities.</i>

1485
01:36:51,824 --> 01:36:54,657
<i>With the unanimous consent
of the Constellations,</i>

1486
01:36:54,699 --> 01:36:57,615
<i>the difficulty level
shall now be raised.</i>

1487
01:36:57,657 --> 01:36:59,490
<i>: What?</i>

1488
01:37:35,699 --> 01:37:37,657
<i>: This wasn't
in the novel.</i>

1489
01:38:06,490 --> 01:38:07,990
Ah...

1490
01:38:14,949 --> 01:38:16,240
Argh!

1491
01:38:20,240 --> 01:38:22,157
Sangah! Quickly, pull him out!

1492
01:38:22,199 --> 01:38:23,615
But then, what about you?

1493
01:38:23,657 --> 01:38:25,615
This will keep me safe
from the flames.

1494
01:38:30,907 --> 01:38:32,949
Now!

1495
01:38:33,949 --> 01:38:36,032
Ahh!

1496
01:38:45,407 --> 01:38:47,657
Ah!

1497
01:39:20,157 --> 01:39:21,782
It's massive!

1498
01:39:23,324 --> 01:39:26,240
Look at that!
It looks like a mantis!

1499
01:39:27,990 --> 01:39:29,490
Gilyeong!

1500
01:39:32,490 --> 01:39:34,782
- Gilyeong...
- But what about Dokja?

1501
01:39:36,199 --> 01:39:37,865
Gilyeong...

1502
01:39:45,865 --> 01:39:47,282
- Ahh!
- Gilyeong, stop.

1503
01:39:47,324 --> 01:39:50,324
I'm okay. I can do it.

1504
01:39:58,782 --> 01:40:00,782
Gilyeong, you've done enough.

1505
01:40:00,824 --> 01:40:03,032
Stop. Stop it, Gilyeong,
please,

1506
01:40:03,074 --> 01:40:04,282
you can't do any more!

1507
01:40:07,824 --> 01:40:09,282
Ah!

1508
01:40:20,365 --> 01:40:23,449
<i>: Lee Hyeonseong's
attribute is ready to blossom.</i>

1509
01:40:24,490 --> 01:40:26,240
Argh!

1510
01:40:40,532 --> 01:40:42,657
Argh!

1511
01:40:55,282 --> 01:40:56,699
Sangah!

1512
01:41:16,699 --> 01:41:18,490
<i>: Lee Hyeonseong
has activated</i>

1513
01:41:18,532 --> 01:41:20,449
<i>Great Mountain Push, level four.</i>

1514
01:41:20,490 --> 01:41:21,657
Argh!

1515
01:41:26,074 --> 01:41:29,074
Hyeonseong,
I'm coming! Ahh!

1516
01:41:34,324 --> 01:41:35,615
Watch out!

1517
01:41:50,740 --> 01:41:53,657
<i>: Somehow, I'll find
a way to face the Fire Dragon.</i>

1518
01:41:53,699 --> 01:41:55,657
But listen to me.

1519
01:41:55,699 --> 01:41:58,199
In the dragon's chest,
there's a round shell,

1520
01:41:58,240 --> 01:41:59,865
and it has a core inside it.

1521
01:41:59,907 --> 01:42:01,407
If we pierce the core,

1522
01:42:01,449 --> 01:42:03,282
we'll defeat the Fire Dragon.

1523
01:42:03,324 --> 01:42:05,282
But the problem is...

1524
01:42:05,324 --> 01:42:07,365
whoever breaks the shell open

1525
01:42:07,407 --> 01:42:10,074
isn't gonna make it out of this.

1526
01:42:10,115 --> 01:42:13,074
If I'm the one who breaks
the shell and I die,

1527
01:42:13,115 --> 01:42:15,282
then Sangah needs to bind
its arms together,

1528
01:42:15,324 --> 01:42:17,407
and Heewon's gotta
pierce the core.

1529
01:42:17,449 --> 01:42:19,074
If you do kill the Dragon,

1530
01:42:19,115 --> 01:42:21,657
you'll receive
a special ability.

1531
01:42:21,699 --> 01:42:23,449
One time only,

1532
01:42:23,490 --> 01:42:25,615
you can bring someone back
from the dead.

1533
01:42:27,324 --> 01:42:29,740
You get what I'm telling you?

1534
01:42:29,782 --> 01:42:32,657
We need to trust each other.

1535
01:42:32,699 --> 01:42:35,365
That's the only way
it's even possible...

1536
01:42:37,282 --> 01:42:38,782
for us all to live.

1537
01:42:46,365 --> 01:42:47,699
Ahh!

1538
01:43:29,865 --> 01:43:31,324
Dokja...

1539
01:43:35,865 --> 01:43:38,074
Heewon! Now!

1540
01:43:43,949 --> 01:43:47,532
Heewon! Quick!

1541
01:44:09,615 --> 01:44:11,324
<i>: The core's shell...</i>

1542
01:44:11,365 --> 01:44:12,615
<i>it's reforming.</i>

1543
01:44:14,490 --> 01:44:16,157
<i>What do we do now?</i>

1544
01:44:32,949 --> 01:44:35,657
The only way
to end this fight...

1545
01:45:33,032 --> 01:45:34,532
<i>: The core's pierced.</i>

1546
01:45:34,574 --> 01:45:37,824
<i>And now Yoo Junghyuk will die.</i>

1547
01:45:37,865 --> 01:45:39,657
<i>Just like in the novel.</i>

1548
01:45:44,907 --> 01:45:47,740
Dokja, what now?

1549
01:46:05,157 --> 01:46:08,574
<i>: The hero is dead.</i>

1550
01:46:09,990 --> 01:46:11,574
<i>I...</i>

1551
01:46:11,615 --> 01:46:13,532
<i>couldn't do anything to stop it.</i>

1552
01:46:14,449 --> 01:46:16,199
<i>: Activating Yoo
Junghyuk's</i>

1553
01:46:16,240 --> 01:46:18,032
<i>Regression skill.</i>

1554
01:46:21,574 --> 01:46:25,532
<i>All matter in the present world
will cease to exist.</i>

1555
01:47:28,907 --> 01:47:32,157
Hey, Bihyeong!
Send me the item! Quick!

1556
01:47:32,199 --> 01:47:34,949
But wait! Dokja,
the world is disintegrating!

1557
01:47:34,990 --> 01:47:36,282
Just send it!

1558
01:47:47,490 --> 01:47:49,532
<i>: Broken Faith
has transformed</i>

1559
01:47:49,574 --> 01:47:51,407
<i>into an Attribute Weapon.</i>

1560
01:47:56,365 --> 01:47:59,324
<i>: I still have a chance.</i>

1561
01:48:02,574 --> 01:48:04,740
Hyeonseong!

1562
01:48:07,532 --> 01:48:08,949
Heewon!

1563
01:48:15,824 --> 01:48:16,865
Sangah!

1564
01:49:05,199 --> 01:49:08,157
<i>: The Green Zone
scenario has been cleared.</i>

1565
01:49:08,199 --> 01:49:11,074
<i>10,000 coins paid as a reward.</i>

1566
01:49:11,115 --> 01:49:12,657
<i>As an additional reward,</i>

1567
01:49:12,699 --> 01:49:15,407
<i>you have received
the King of No Killing.</i>

1568
01:49:15,449 --> 01:49:19,907
<i>Kim Dokja revived Yoo Junghyuk
using the King of No Killing.</i>

1569
01:49:31,407 --> 01:49:32,782
We won!

1570
01:49:36,407 --> 01:49:39,324
Yeah, haha! Ya-hoo!

1571
01:49:41,199 --> 01:49:42,865
We took all those bastards down!

1572
01:49:42,907 --> 01:49:44,365
<i>: Yoo Junghyuk.</i>

1573
01:49:46,032 --> 01:49:47,574
<i>Are you okay?</i>

1574
01:49:49,532 --> 01:49:51,782
<i>: I didn't think
you could do it.</i>

1575
01:50:11,782 --> 01:50:14,449
Whoa, nice work!
We kicked their asses, huh?

1576
01:50:25,157 --> 01:50:27,407
Nice work with that sword,
Dokja.

1577
01:50:27,449 --> 01:50:29,240
Guess it wasn't broken
after all.

1578
01:50:29,282 --> 01:50:31,782
And Hyeonseong,
your skills were badass.

1579
01:50:31,824 --> 01:50:34,199
I only wish
I'd stepped in sooner.

1580
01:50:34,240 --> 01:50:36,074
But all of us did great.

1581
01:50:38,282 --> 01:50:40,782
<i>:
I, who was truly nothing,</i>

1582
01:50:40,824 --> 01:50:42,657
<i>lived this story,</i>

1583
01:50:42,699 --> 01:50:44,699
<i>and met new friends.</i>

1584
01:50:45,574 --> 01:50:47,824
<i>And together, as a team,</i>

1585
01:50:47,865 --> 01:50:50,990
<i>we can write a new ending.</i>

1586
01:51:51,115 --> 01:51:53,990
<i>: A new scenario
is starting.</i>

1587
01:51:54,032 --> 01:51:56,824
<i>All of the barriers
have been lifted.</i>

1588
01:51:58,532 --> 01:52:01,907
Help me!
Somebody help! Help!

1589
01:52:01,949 --> 01:52:03,824
Whoa!

1590
01:52:03,865 --> 01:52:05,949
Mr. Han?

1591
01:52:05,990 --> 01:52:09,115
Watch out! They killed
everyone at Geumho Station!

1592
01:52:09,157 --> 01:52:10,865
Even the children
and the elderly,

1593
01:52:10,907 --> 01:52:12,865
they killed them!

1594
01:52:12,907 --> 01:52:14,949
Don't just stand there, come on!

1595
01:52:14,990 --> 01:52:17,782
They're on their way here now!

1596
01:52:19,282 --> 01:52:21,657
That's them,
they're almost here!

1597
01:52:22,074 --> 01:52:24,574
<i>: Wait, already?</i>

1598
01:52:33,115 --> 01:52:34,865
They're coming.
They're coming!

1599
01:52:49,990 --> 01:52:53,657
Subtitling: difuze

